1
00:00:03,780 --> 00:02:03,780
Please contact turkision@gmail.com for any inquiries

2
00:02:03,985 --> 00:02:07,785
No living being was harmed during the
filming of this series.

3
00:02:08,264 --> 00:02:11,135
Marmaracık Castle

4
00:02:11,375 --> 00:02:15,395
Episode 105

5
00:02:22,585 --> 00:02:25,195
The spoils of the castle, Turgut Bey.

6
00:02:28,125 --> 00:02:31,765
To whom do you think our Bey
will give the castle, brother?

7
00:02:32,115 --> 00:02:36,025
Marmaracık...

8
00:02:41,945 --> 00:02:43,905
belongs to Turgut Bey the most.

9
00:02:45,105 --> 00:02:47,665
Do you think we deserve it, JCerkutay?

10
00:02:47,935 --> 00:02:50,755
Will my Bey find someone better than you?

11
00:02:52,155 --> 00:02:54,005
This place belongs to you.

12
00:02:54,755 --> 00:02:56,075
Thank you.

13
00:02:56,985 --> 00:02:58,495
Thank you, Cerkutay.

14
00:03:09,465 --> 00:03:12,965
Mashallah!

15
00:03:13,235 --> 00:03:15,685
Mashallah!

16
00:03:17,595 --> 00:03:20,315
This castle is full of treasures.

17
00:03:29,585 --> 00:03:32,655
Osman Bey takes this for himself.

18
00:03:33,175 --> 00:03:37,415
Turgut Bey, he'll give
you this, it's your right.

19
00:03:38,255 --> 00:03:42,175
This is for me.

20
00:03:44,195 --> 00:03:48,705
What do you give out before
Osman Bey comes, Bayındır Bey?

21
00:03:54,965 --> 00:03:56,705
Where is Osman Bey?

22
00:03:56,735 --> 00:03:58,385
I don't know where Osman Bey is.

23
00:03:58,435 --> 00:04:00,285
Allah knows when he will come.

24
00:04:00,285 --> 00:04:02,125
But what are you doing?

25
00:04:03,955 --> 00:04:09,045
Well, then let's enlarge that
barn...

26
00:04:09,375 --> 00:04:11,575
Our horses are
many, and the barn is small.

27
00:04:11,645 --> 00:04:12,965
No, no.

28
00:04:13,115 --> 00:04:14,605
We do what it takes.

29
00:04:14,605 --> 00:04:16,144
You go back to your stall.

30
00:04:16,185 --> 00:04:19,445
It's time to trade, don't
lose your gold coins.

31
00:04:19,695 --> 00:04:21,084
Come on.

32
00:04:23,575 --> 00:04:25,715
Isn't there anyone to look after
your stall?

33
00:04:26,435 --> 00:04:27,875
Lots of work here.

34
00:04:30,345 --> 00:04:32,185
Go back to your work.

35
00:04:32,715 --> 00:04:34,695
You have no business here, Bayındır Bey.

36
00:04:36,885 --> 00:04:39,035
As for us, we have a lot of work, Beys.

37
00:04:40,665 --> 00:04:42,905
Come on, move, valiants.

38
00:04:46,415 --> 00:04:48,475
What are you striving for?

39
00:04:49,025 --> 00:04:51,275
And where is Osman Bey?

40
00:04:53,045 --> 00:04:56,165
I'm going back to my stall, however...

41
00:04:56,665 --> 00:04:59,235
If you do something against my interest...

42
00:05:00,265 --> 00:05:02,665
I will demolish the
world above your heads.

43
00:05:05,615 --> 00:05:06,985
Come on.

44
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:41,255
Yenişehir

45
00:05:44,590 --> 00:05:47,570
Thank Allah, my two sons have set
off on the Karacahisar road.

46
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:50,530
I'm happy that they are together.

47
00:05:50,620 --> 00:05:53,360
A brother certainly carries
his brother's burden.

48
00:05:54,130 --> 00:05:56,100
Do not worry.

49
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:57,930
They will protect each other well.

50
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:01,140
How are the setups, Ülgen?

51
00:06:01,170 --> 00:06:03,310
We put provisions on top
of the carriage, Malhun Hatun.

52
00:06:03,350 --> 00:06:05,680
We have no shortage, thank Allah.

53
00:06:06,610 --> 00:06:09,750
Alps, be careful.

54
00:06:09,980 --> 00:06:11,620
Your command, Malhun Hatun.

55
00:06:29,870 --> 00:06:32,210
What are you
thinking about, Malhun Hatun?

56
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:34,840
Have you started to
miss your son now?

57
00:06:35,750 --> 00:06:39,230
I think of Osman Bey, he
summoned us, but...

58
00:06:39,950 --> 00:06:42,070
He is not in Marmaracık.

59
00:06:42,260 --> 00:06:44,400
He did not tell anyone where he was.

60
00:06:45,350 --> 00:06:46,880
I got worried.

61
00:06:53,780 --> 00:06:57,400
Near Kopruhisar

62
00:07:00,100 --> 00:07:02,230
My dad used to say...

63
00:07:03,430 --> 00:07:07,050
"as long as we do not have the judgment of
this world..."

64
00:07:07,170 --> 00:07:10,040
"you don't ever have to be hesitant."

65
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:21,190
Are the valiants here?

66
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:27,870
Are the keepers of secrets here?

67
00:07:33,290 --> 00:07:34,980
You can appear now.

68
00:07:38,630 --> 00:07:40,270
My Osman Bey.

69
00:07:52,990 --> 00:07:54,930
Salam Alaikum, my Bey.

70
00:07:55,020 --> 00:07:56,590
Alaikum Salam.

71
00:07:56,660 --> 00:07:58,750
May Allah bless my valiant.

72
00:07:59,010 --> 00:08:01,240
- Let me kiss your hand.
- No.

73
00:08:07,350 --> 00:08:08,860
Gürbüz.

74
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:10,650
Tell me, is the task completed?

75
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:12,190
Completed, my Bey.

76
00:08:17,010 --> 00:08:19,020
Now is the time.

77
00:08:21,610 --> 00:08:23,900
Marmaracık opened the door of conquests.

78
00:08:24,820 --> 00:08:28,010
And now, we're going to open Köprühisar.

79
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:30,390
My Bey, command me.

80
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:31,970
We do what you say.

81
00:08:31,970 --> 00:08:33,900
We are always at your command.

82
00:08:34,730 --> 00:08:36,409
Yes, you are behind us.

83
00:08:36,808 --> 00:08:38,600
Standing water may become cloudy.

84
00:08:38,650 --> 00:08:40,940
But the flowing water does not get dirty.

85
00:08:40,990 --> 00:08:43,610
We will become a roaring
torrent and head towards them.

86
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:45,820
Tell me now.

87
00:08:47,790 --> 00:08:49,620
How are things in Köpruhisar?

88
00:09:41,890 --> 00:09:43,610
Do you eat all this food?

89
00:09:44,220 --> 00:09:47,470
My Bey, a hungry horse can not walk.

90
00:09:47,820 --> 00:09:51,420
Weak iron can not break the enemy.

91
00:10:16,190 --> 00:10:17,720
Since the map is right there...

92
00:10:17,910 --> 00:10:20,490
There must be important things to tell me.

93
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:29,790
Yes, my Bey.

94
00:10:40,610 --> 00:10:43,110
Look at Turgut Bey.

95
00:10:44,460 --> 00:10:47,670
He thinks he attacks
the infidels on his own.

96
00:10:47,760 --> 00:10:49,330
He thinks he fights alone.

97
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:54,400
Could they have passed the
cross without me, Hüseyin?

98
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:56,170
They wouldn't have
been able to do that.

99
00:10:56,210 --> 00:10:58,450
Yes, they wouldn't have crossed.

100
00:11:02,590 --> 00:11:05,180
But, they will see from now on.

101
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:06,910
My name...

102
00:11:22,110 --> 00:11:25,310
Bayındır always gets into trouble.

103
00:11:29,270 --> 00:11:30,710
Alps.

104
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:34,970
Draw your swords.

105
00:11:54,990 --> 00:11:57,150
Who are you? And what do you want?

106
00:11:57,840 --> 00:12:00,370
What we want is an agreement with you.

107
00:12:01,230 --> 00:12:03,520
For this reason, you must stop.

108
00:12:12,220 --> 00:12:16,490
Are you a human or a fairy?
I don't know your features.

109
00:12:18,110 --> 00:12:21,010
Why would I agree with you?

110
00:12:21,450 --> 00:12:24,270
I'll take you to Olof.

111
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:31,240
Let me see your face that you
hide behind this mask first.

112
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:49,630
You are Marta, the
nice cloth seller in Yenişehir, right?

113
00:12:49,740 --> 00:12:52,870
No, I'm Frigg.

114
00:12:53,190 --> 00:12:54,880
My name is Frigg.

115
00:12:55,100 --> 00:12:57,120
Are you that demon?

116
00:12:58,290 --> 00:13:00,350
Olof's sweetheart?

117
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:07,170
What does Olof want
to agree with me?

118
00:13:07,750 --> 00:13:09,540
You should talk to him.

119
00:13:11,870 --> 00:13:17,920
In addition to everything I know, I
now know the face behind the mask.

120
00:13:18,890 --> 00:13:23,740
Be careful not to make a wrong move
against me, or I will burn you all.

121
00:13:26,020 --> 00:13:28,620
I also know a lot of things.

122
00:13:28,810 --> 00:13:33,090
For example, it was you who stole the
gold from Olof, Bayındır Bey.

123
00:13:34,450 --> 00:13:36,110
What do you know?

124
00:13:36,260 --> 00:13:39,330
What I know about you may kill you.

125
00:13:40,670 --> 00:13:46,000
But Olof summons you alive to his side.

126
00:13:55,420 --> 00:13:58,150
Make up your mind now, Bayındır.

127
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:03,980
Either I kill you here, or
we go together to Olof.

128
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:10,270
As long as you don't kill me while you have
the chance...

129
00:14:11,430 --> 00:14:15,140
It means you need me, lady.

130
00:14:16,470 --> 00:14:21,960
Well, come on, let's go to
Olof and see what's wrong with him.

131
00:14:47,895 --> 00:14:51,035
So the conquest of Marmaracık
has put them in a terrible state.

132
00:14:52,225 --> 00:14:54,665
Their hearts tremble with fear.

133
00:14:54,975 --> 00:14:57,925
But this fear of theirs
will increase their caution.

134
00:14:58,655 --> 00:15:04,365
They have written a letter to the emperor
and are waiting for support.

135
00:15:04,835 --> 00:15:07,525
Yes, they are afraid.

136
00:15:07,855 --> 00:15:14,005
They saw how we went to İnegol after Bilecik,
they know that we will now go to Köprühisar.

137
00:15:15,505 --> 00:15:17,215
Tell me what's the situation now.

138
00:15:17,315 --> 00:15:23,135
They gather blacksmiths from the villages
to repair the walls.

139
00:15:24,615 --> 00:15:30,155
They gather the workers and discourage
them from their work to dig trenches.

140
00:15:36,135 --> 00:15:38,975
In addition, they have increased
the soldiers' patrols.

141
00:15:51,695 --> 00:15:55,795
What is this outfit, Marcus?

142
00:16:00,085 --> 00:16:01,595
Osman.

143
00:16:03,315 --> 00:16:04,895
Attack!

144
00:16:05,015 --> 00:16:06,775
You know what you're going to do.

145
00:16:09,595 --> 00:16:10,985
Come on!

146
00:16:41,395 --> 00:16:42,785
Spread out!

147
00:17:12,185 --> 00:17:13,755
From here, from here.

148
00:18:18,435 --> 00:18:22,985
- Let me go now, my Bey.
- No, you will come with me to Marmarcık.

149
00:18:23,485 --> 00:18:27,525
See what happens after you have turned
the castle of the infidels into a homeland for the Turks.

150
00:18:27,655 --> 00:18:31,015
- Come on.
- Your command, my Bey.

151
00:18:32,125 --> 00:18:39,205
The best type of food is halal food.

152
00:18:39,705 --> 00:18:43,175
Let us go back to our city so that
I may eat there to my fill.

153
00:18:45,545 --> 00:18:46,905
Come on.

154
00:18:48,685 --> 00:18:50,865
Öktem Tribe

155
00:18:51,585 --> 00:18:53,125
Alçiçek.

156
00:18:53,990 --> 00:18:57,140
Is there any news about the Alps?
Has Osman Bey returned to town?

157
00:18:57,150 --> 00:18:58,460
No, father.

158
00:18:58,880 --> 00:19:03,030
And he did not come back in the evening
either. Our Alps are still waiting for him.

159
00:19:07,150 --> 00:19:11,950
Osman doesn't stop and runs
his affairs unobtrusively.

160
00:19:13,040 --> 00:19:16,450
And you sit here and wait for
him to fight and conquer.

161
00:19:17,280 --> 00:19:19,100
Bayındır is also out of sight.

162
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:28,030
They're doing something
behind us, however...

163
00:19:31,100 --> 00:19:33,660
This calm does not bode well.

164
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:39,330
What did Osman do to
benefit us until today, Öktem Bey?

165
00:19:41,110 --> 00:19:43,940
Let's see what misfortune
he will bring us again.

166
00:19:44,790 --> 00:19:48,690
May I come in, my Bey?
Subasi Aktemur wants to see you.

167
00:19:55,470 --> 00:19:57,150
Let him in.

168
00:20:03,490 --> 00:20:06,560
- Salam Alaikum.
- Alaikum Salam.

169
00:20:13,490 --> 00:20:14,750
Lower your head.

170
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:25,120
Speak, Subasi.

171
00:20:26,690 --> 00:20:29,050
I brought you the
greetings of Osman Bey.

172
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:34,820
Osman Bey
is waiting for you in Marmaracık Castle.

173
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,580
Marmaracık?

174
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:52,660
Marmaracık is now
owned by the Turks.

175
00:20:57,980 --> 00:21:00,580
Osman Bey conquered Marmaracık.

176
00:21:10,050 --> 00:21:12,890
He invites all Beys to his
council in the evening.

177
00:21:14,430 --> 00:21:16,900
He is waiting for you in his new land.

178
00:21:19,280 --> 00:21:20,860
Thank you.

179
00:21:34,250 --> 00:21:35,420
Leave me.

180
00:21:55,690 --> 00:22:00,180
You have stolen my gold
and killed my men, Bayındır.

181
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:05,700
If I considered you my
enemy, I would kill you.

182
00:22:06,080 --> 00:22:10,180
Trust that this axe would have
split your head.

183
00:22:11,480 --> 00:22:14,170
I know everything you did.

184
00:22:14,870 --> 00:22:17,590
Your gold was loose cash.

185
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:22,080
If you protected it, it wouldn't have
gone to someone else.

186
00:22:22,760 --> 00:22:24,890
Stop.

187
00:22:25,640 --> 00:22:30,270
Well, then tell me why
you invited me here.

188
00:22:31,480 --> 00:22:35,560
What I want is to have a deal with you.

189
00:22:36,010 --> 00:22:40,330
And move together against Osman.

190
00:22:41,880 --> 00:22:44,380
Oh my.

191
00:22:47,150 --> 00:22:52,280
Why am I even helping you, Olof?

192
00:22:53,110 --> 00:22:54,680
Who are you?

193
00:22:55,840 --> 00:22:57,560
Who are you?

194
00:22:58,340 --> 00:23:01,180
You think I will deceive the
great Bey Osman.

195
00:23:02,400 --> 00:23:03,400
Choose correctly.

196
00:23:04,240 --> 00:23:05,240
Stand by me.

197
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:11,480
Otherwise, you too will lose with Osman.

198
00:23:12,100 --> 00:23:13,680
I...

199
00:23:14,630 --> 00:23:16,160
I don't take the losing side.

200
00:23:16,590 --> 00:23:18,570
Don't tire yourself in vain.

201
00:23:23,710 --> 00:23:24,710
Bring it.

202
00:23:50,590 --> 00:23:51,880
This gold is for you.

203
00:23:56,820 --> 00:24:00,070
Are you going to fool
me with this little thing?

204
00:24:00,740 --> 00:24:03,440
My treasures are like the sea.

205
00:24:04,890 --> 00:24:07,810
This is just a drop of it.

206
00:24:09,280 --> 00:24:11,480
Don't tire yourself.

207
00:24:12,500 --> 00:24:17,660
I earn a thousand times of it from
the conquests with Osman Bey

208
00:24:19,670 --> 00:24:22,550
His spoils are many, thank Allah.

209
00:24:24,230 --> 00:24:26,600
Do you think Osman
will give you his spoils?

210
00:24:27,470 --> 00:24:28,660
He is using you.

211
00:24:28,950 --> 00:24:33,670
You put your life and your goods
for Osman to take Marmaracık.

212
00:24:34,870 --> 00:24:35,980
So what will he do?

213
00:24:37,710 --> 00:24:39,970
Who do you think he will
give Marmaracık to?

214
00:24:41,670 --> 00:24:43,540
This issue is between us.

215
00:24:46,380 --> 00:24:49,970
This issue doesn't concern you.

216
00:24:50,490 --> 00:24:53,490
Don't worry in vain, woman.

217
00:24:57,320 --> 00:25:00,350
Suppose that I accept your offer...

218
00:25:02,910 --> 00:25:04,590
So what do I gain from that?

219
00:25:04,690 --> 00:25:06,630
Half of my treasures.

220
00:25:07,570 --> 00:25:09,460
Not only that...

221
00:25:10,920 --> 00:25:15,670
I will share with you my treasure found
in Constantinople.

222
00:25:17,440 --> 00:25:19,350
Osman Bey is very important.

223
00:25:23,940 --> 00:25:25,130
However...

224
00:25:26,170 --> 00:25:27,980
Gold is also very important.

225
00:25:30,820 --> 00:25:32,020
That is what I mean

226
00:25:33,040 --> 00:25:36,920
Such issues can not be
decided immediately.

227
00:25:37,680 --> 00:25:40,270
Give me time to think.

228
00:25:40,790 --> 00:25:42,900
I will inform you of my
decision in the evening.

229
00:25:43,970 --> 00:25:45,270
Think.

230
00:25:46,050 --> 00:25:47,610
Think, but...

231
00:25:49,310 --> 00:25:51,020
If you try to sell us...

232
00:25:52,740 --> 00:25:54,750
My axe will not miss you this time.

233
00:25:56,000 --> 00:25:57,300
Don't forget this.

234
00:25:59,150 --> 00:26:00,650
Sir Olof.

235
00:26:02,390 --> 00:26:06,150
It's hard for you to catch me
in a moment of weakness again.

236
00:26:08,700 --> 00:26:13,840
If your strength is sufficient for my
hundred knights, do as you say.

237
00:26:18,470 --> 00:26:19,970
Take this.

238
00:26:20,590 --> 00:26:22,390
Give me a blindfold, come on.

239
00:26:30,760 --> 00:26:32,460
Come on, take me, come on.

240
00:26:36,390 --> 00:26:38,160
Bayındır's work is easy.

241
00:26:40,360 --> 00:26:45,370
Osman must have some weaknesses.

242
00:26:48,200 --> 00:26:50,530
I will finish him when I find it.

243
00:26:53,290 --> 00:26:56,490
Think of everyone around
Osman as Bayındır.

244
00:26:57,190 --> 00:26:59,990
If only we could sow the seeds
of jealousy among them...

245
00:27:00,640 --> 00:27:03,190
They will solve the
Yenişehir issue themselves.

246
00:27:03,890 --> 00:27:06,720
You made your greatest weapon
speak, my love.

247
00:27:07,730 --> 00:27:11,920
No one can be as smart as you.

248
00:27:15,140 --> 00:27:17,730
Marmaracık Castle

249
00:27:20,600 --> 00:27:23,180
We'll take a thousand castles like you.

250
00:27:24,610 --> 00:27:27,680
This castle will pave the way
for all castles, Inshallah

251
00:27:32,910 --> 00:27:36,330
Who is good at war will own it.

252
00:27:40,080 --> 00:27:48,860
But is there anyone
more clever than me?

253
00:27:49,810 --> 00:27:54,140
You've been after raids
for years, Turgut.

254
00:27:56,180 --> 00:28:03,520
Kingship is right for those who
irrigated this land with their blood.

255
00:28:16,420 --> 00:28:17,720
My Allah.

256
00:28:19,150 --> 00:28:22,740
Let me rule the Marmaracık Castle.

257
00:28:31,660 --> 00:28:32,960
Forgiveness of Allah.

258
00:28:35,460 --> 00:28:36,760
Forgiveness of Allah.

259
00:28:37,680 --> 00:28:39,420
What are you saying, Turgut?

260
00:28:40,320 --> 00:28:42,030
Who gave you this right?

261
00:28:42,440 --> 00:28:45,260
Did Osman Bey
tell you to take this castle for yourself?

262
00:28:46,340 --> 00:28:48,400
So what do you tell yourself?

263
00:29:07,770 --> 00:29:09,270
Oh my!

264
00:29:11,110 --> 00:29:13,130
The throne has met you well, Turgut Bey.

265
00:29:16,310 --> 00:29:18,110
But don't get too attached to it.

266
00:29:18,790 --> 00:29:20,810
You know we don't settle in one place.

267
00:29:21,670 --> 00:29:23,690
This is not what I'm after, Brother Boran.

268
00:29:23,740 --> 00:29:26,930
You know we don't have time to sit on
it because of the conquests.

269
00:29:27,100 --> 00:29:28,600
Turgut Bey.

270
00:29:31,440 --> 00:29:34,320
Inshallah, Osman Bey will give
you the rule of the castle.

271
00:29:39,800 --> 00:29:41,100
Thank you.

272
00:29:42,330 --> 00:29:43,630
Allah knows.

273
00:29:44,950 --> 00:29:46,450
We'll see, brother.

274
00:30:06,550 --> 00:30:08,260
You see, Öktem Bey?

275
00:30:08,680 --> 00:30:11,480
You were saying that Osman Bey
and I will take Marmaracık.

276
00:30:11,940 --> 00:30:15,030
He does not rest while
you sit in the tribe.

277
00:30:15,590 --> 00:30:17,950
If he did it in secret...

278
00:30:19,920 --> 00:30:21,740
There must be something he knows.

279
00:30:23,960 --> 00:30:25,820
Let's get to Marmaracık.

280
00:30:26,710 --> 00:30:28,300
And we'll know what it is.

281
00:30:29,810 --> 00:30:31,310
And what will it be?

282
00:30:31,680 --> 00:30:34,180
He summoned us to show us his power.

283
00:30:42,120 --> 00:30:44,160
Is your wound healed, Subasi?

284
00:30:46,440 --> 00:30:49,110
The answer depends on the
wound you are asking about.

285
00:30:51,290 --> 00:30:53,860
Some wounds never heal, Alçiçek Hatun.

286
00:30:56,080 --> 00:30:57,970
Does your soul burn a lot?

287
00:31:09,050 --> 00:31:12,320
- Salam Alaikum.
- Alaikum Salam.

288
00:31:13,510 --> 00:31:16,080
Well, where are you going, Öktem bey?

289
00:31:16,170 --> 00:31:17,670
You and your family?

290
00:31:20,860 --> 00:31:23,050
Osman Bey has summoned us to Marmaracık.

291
00:31:25,640 --> 00:31:28,150
We're going there, don't you
know about that?

292
00:31:35,230 --> 00:31:36,480
No.

293
00:31:37,100 --> 00:31:38,950
Nobody told us anything.

294
00:31:43,420 --> 00:31:44,960
Subasi.

295
00:31:46,970 --> 00:31:48,810
Do you know why we weren't summoned?

296
00:31:49,840 --> 00:31:53,370
I don't know, my mission is
to summon Öktem Bey.

297
00:32:02,230 --> 00:32:04,750
Come over this side, Alçiçek.

298
00:32:17,820 --> 00:32:19,530
I'm watching you, Alçiçek.

299
00:32:22,520 --> 00:32:24,300
Act accordingly.

300
00:32:28,500 --> 00:32:30,000
Okay then.

301
00:32:31,230 --> 00:32:32,810
May Allah make your path easy.

302
00:32:33,200 --> 00:32:35,580
Thank you, Bayındır.

303
00:32:54,610 --> 00:32:56,670
Oh, Osman Bey.

304
00:32:58,570 --> 00:33:00,450
You take the Castle with me but...

305
00:33:01,310 --> 00:33:03,640
you don't pay any
attention to my existence.

306
00:33:06,230 --> 00:33:08,270
And you
do not summon me to your court.

307
00:33:09,840 --> 00:33:11,490
And the feast is held without us.

308
00:33:13,530 --> 00:33:15,370
Does such a thing
make sense, Hüseyin?

309
00:33:15,490 --> 00:33:16,990
No, my Bey.

310
00:33:17,020 --> 00:33:18,780
To whom the castle belongs?

311
00:33:21,790 --> 00:33:24,270
We are the ones who paved
the way for the conquest.

312
00:33:24,820 --> 00:33:28,550
What will happen if you don't give the
castle to the one who helped you?

313
00:33:29,880 --> 00:33:32,380
There have been a lot of gold chests.

314
00:33:33,690 --> 00:33:35,530
They didn't give us our share of it.

315
00:33:36,060 --> 00:33:39,840
They said "go to your stall in
the market."

316
00:33:42,060 --> 00:33:47,090
They see that the jacket of the
conquest is only worthy of them.

317
00:33:48,430 --> 00:33:52,660
I will rip it off
while they are wearing it...

318
00:33:53,430 --> 00:33:55,550
I will.

319
00:33:57,160 --> 00:33:58,880
What are we going to do, my Bey?

320
00:33:59,000 --> 00:34:01,450
As long as they see us
as less than them...

321
00:34:02,070 --> 00:34:06,560
I will burn the ground under their
feet and turn it into hell.

322
00:34:07,830 --> 00:34:11,630
Why do you frown instead of
thanking us that you are alive?

323
00:34:13,989 --> 00:34:16,260
I look what you did to the castle...

324
00:34:17,530 --> 00:34:19,030
It's a tragedy.

325
00:34:21,800 --> 00:34:24,469
But this tragedy, like any
tragedy, will end in blood.

326
00:34:24,500 --> 00:34:26,750
And it will be your blood
that will be shed.

327
00:34:31,460 --> 00:34:33,250
Look at those flags.

328
00:34:35,750 --> 00:34:38,290
We don't attach it anywhere
we haven't seen blood.

329
00:34:38,820 --> 00:34:41,510
Beware that the blood
that will be shed is your own.

330
00:34:42,949 --> 00:34:44,800
And look at these valiants.

331
00:34:46,040 --> 00:34:48,360
They are running towards death laughing.

332
00:34:51,429 --> 00:34:54,080
Don't forget, Kantakuzenos.

333
00:34:54,870 --> 00:34:57,360
When Osman Bey sends you
to Constantinople...

334
00:34:57,520 --> 00:34:59,630
keep your lands there.

335
00:34:59,720 --> 00:35:01,910
Because we will come and take it all.

336
00:35:04,520 --> 00:35:06,480
I suggest you do the same.

337
00:35:07,300 --> 00:35:10,360
I will take back everything
that belongs to us.

338
00:35:10,820 --> 00:35:12,280
Even more than that.

339
00:35:13,600 --> 00:35:14,640
We'll see...

340
00:35:14,820 --> 00:35:16,100
Prince.

341
00:35:16,440 --> 00:35:17,460
We'll see.

342
00:35:17,830 --> 00:35:19,420
We'll see, Turgut Bey.

343
00:35:19,650 --> 00:35:21,160
Osman Bey is coming.

344
00:35:21,250 --> 00:35:22,760
Osman Bey is coming.

345
00:35:22,870 --> 00:35:24,660
Osman Bey is coming.

346
00:35:40,020 --> 00:35:41,610
Salam Alaikum.

347
00:35:41,670 --> 00:35:43,240
Alaikum Salam.

348
00:35:51,130 --> 00:35:52,840
Mashallah.

349
00:35:52,880 --> 00:35:55,470
These flags are what a homeland
should have.

350
00:35:57,890 --> 00:35:59,420
Thank Allah.

351
00:35:59,520 --> 00:36:01,560
You put it everywhere

352
00:36:02,080 --> 00:36:03,580
Thank Allah.

353
00:36:19,040 --> 00:36:21,630
Welcome, all, to our blessed
celebration today.

354
00:36:23,810 --> 00:36:24,950
Alps!

355
00:36:26,160 --> 00:36:28,690
Meet your brother, Gürbüz Alp.

356
00:36:44,770 --> 00:36:45,860
Turgut Bey.

357
00:36:46,640 --> 00:36:48,100
Welcome, Brother Gürbüz.

358
00:36:48,130 --> 00:36:49,500
Thank you.

359
00:36:49,530 --> 00:36:51,110
Welcome, my brother

360
00:36:53,540 --> 00:36:56,220
Marmaracık is as ready from the outside
as it is from the inside, Osman Bey.

361
00:36:56,240 --> 00:36:58,130
Valiants have made a great effort.

362
00:36:58,310 --> 00:37:00,360
And the ladies worked a lot, Mashallah.

363
00:37:00,440 --> 00:37:01,940
Thank you.

364
00:37:02,790 --> 00:37:04,580
Welcome, Gürbüz Alp.

365
00:37:04,670 --> 00:37:05,780
Thank you.

366
00:37:05,820 --> 00:37:07,410
Where have you been performing
your mission, brother?

367
00:37:07,450 --> 00:37:09,680
You'll hear about it when
the time is right.

368
00:37:09,780 --> 00:37:11,130
Okay.

369
00:37:12,200 --> 00:37:14,700
Your secret is as big as
you, isn't it, brother?

370
00:37:18,130 --> 00:37:20,170
Let's see how much you weigh.

371
00:37:23,320 --> 00:37:26,080
I will smash your head.

372
00:37:26,240 --> 00:37:30,750
Then we will be at the same level.

373
00:37:33,910 --> 00:37:35,460
Mashallah.

374
00:37:38,740 --> 00:37:40,440
Where is Bayındır Bey?

375
00:37:43,160 --> 00:37:45,320
He didn't know when you were coming.

376
00:37:45,430 --> 00:37:47,930
I found him dividing the
spoils of his own accord.

377
00:37:49,440 --> 00:37:51,000
I asked him to go to work.

378
00:37:51,240 --> 00:37:53,360
But he will surely come
in the evening.

379
00:37:57,440 --> 00:37:58,820
You made a mistake.

380
00:38:02,740 --> 00:38:06,980
No one shall be dismissed from the place
of conquest before they get their booty.

381
00:38:08,210 --> 00:38:09,430
Okay, Osman Bey.

382
00:38:10,530 --> 00:38:12,030
It's true what you say.

383
00:38:20,470 --> 00:38:23,540
Yenişehir

384
00:38:26,985 --> 00:38:28,515
Welcome, my Bey.

385
00:38:28,555 --> 00:38:30,365
Oh my! The market is crowded.

386
00:38:30,395 --> 00:38:32,185
Business is going well.

387
00:38:32,235 --> 00:38:34,475
Don't talk nonsense and
get outside, come on!

388
00:38:44,295 --> 00:38:47,485
The man is having a feast in his castle.

389
00:38:47,855 --> 00:38:49,435
And his market is working.

390
00:38:50,425 --> 00:38:54,535
He earns money with
ease while sitting in his place.

391
00:39:00,715 --> 00:39:05,345
And Bayındır helps him when he needs him.

392
00:39:06,905 --> 00:39:08,425
But wait!

393
00:39:09,815 --> 00:39:12,055
There will be a day
when it's the opposite.

394
00:39:13,005 --> 00:39:15,085
Then it will be my turn.

395
00:39:16,205 --> 00:39:17,975
Suppose that...

396
00:39:18,425 --> 00:39:20,715
I accepted Olof's offer.

397
00:39:21,545 --> 00:39:23,675
So what are you going to do?

398
00:39:24,955 --> 00:39:27,005
Repentance! I seek forgiveness from Allah!

399
00:39:27,175 --> 00:39:29,275
Repentance! I seek forgiveness from Allah!

400
00:39:30,185 --> 00:39:32,665
Go write what I'm going
to dictate to you, come on.

401
00:39:39,065 --> 00:39:40,605
Come on, Hüseyin.

402
00:39:44,575 --> 00:39:46,745
The sun of the Seljuks...

403
00:39:48,055 --> 00:39:49,605
Valide Sultan.

404
00:40:10,395 --> 00:40:12,535
Tell me what are your requests?

405
00:40:13,055 --> 00:40:16,355
We knew you'd take this place one day.

406
00:40:20,965 --> 00:40:22,935
Is this a white day... (good)

407
00:40:22,985 --> 00:40:24,985
or black? (bad)

408
00:40:26,845 --> 00:40:29,535
Is our arrival a salvation for you?

409
00:40:29,915 --> 00:40:31,535
Or is it injustice?

410
00:40:32,045 --> 00:40:36,735
You are the one who will show
us if it is a black or white day.

411
00:40:37,735 --> 00:40:39,125
No.

412
00:40:39,935 --> 00:40:41,465
Your souls...

413
00:40:44,295 --> 00:40:47,835
and your possessions and
beliefs are in my trust.

414
00:40:51,675 --> 00:40:53,495
No one will be harmed.

415
00:40:54,295 --> 00:40:56,315
You will live freely.

416
00:40:57,485 --> 00:41:01,145
And what about taxes?
We hear you're lowering it.

417
00:41:01,975 --> 00:41:05,085
You have heard of the welfare
that our government brings.

418
00:41:05,915 --> 00:41:08,715
Never worry, we'll cut it all down.

419
00:41:10,135 --> 00:41:12,095
You were in the lead that day.

420
00:41:12,715 --> 00:41:15,415
Are you the one who will
become the ruler of the castle?

421
00:41:17,995 --> 00:41:19,785
I haven't made up my mind yet.

422
00:41:24,605 --> 00:41:27,895
Everyone will know when the time comes.

423
00:41:35,935 --> 00:41:37,715
The food is ripe.

424
00:41:40,275 --> 00:41:41,655
I'll wait

425
00:41:41,995 --> 00:41:44,555
Let the flesh ripen so that I
may devour it.

426
00:41:44,825 --> 00:41:46,395
Cerguday.

427
00:41:50,555 --> 00:41:52,085
Cerguday.

428
00:41:53,765 --> 00:41:55,135
I do not hear.

429
00:41:55,155 --> 00:41:56,455
As you know.

430
00:41:56,495 --> 00:41:58,185
- I know, I know.
- I don't hear.

431
00:41:58,205 --> 00:42:00,205
I know you don't hear.

432
00:42:01,005 --> 00:42:03,535
Fortunately, you don't hear, if you did...

433
00:42:04,535 --> 00:42:06,855
would you stay here...

434
00:42:09,755 --> 00:42:11,615
if you heard what Osman Bey said?

435
00:42:16,445 --> 00:42:18,305
My ears are deaf, however...

436
00:42:19,415 --> 00:42:21,205
Come on, I'm listening to you.

437
00:42:21,225 --> 00:42:23,295
Come on, tell me, talk.

438
00:42:23,335 --> 00:42:24,785
What did he say?

439
00:42:24,805 --> 00:42:28,305
Why would I tell a man
who doesn't hear anything?

440
00:42:30,205 --> 00:42:32,215
But I've heard terrible things.

441
00:42:33,245 --> 00:42:35,615
You're burned, Cerguday, you're burned.

442
00:42:49,255 --> 00:42:50,615
What did he say?

443
00:42:50,685 --> 00:42:52,415
Did he talk about me?

444
00:42:52,985 --> 00:42:54,325
Did my Bey talk about me?

445
00:42:55,115 --> 00:42:57,625
What did he say, Ülgen Hatun?
Don't let me explode.

446
00:42:58,505 --> 00:43:00,055
What, Cerguday?

447
00:43:00,115 --> 00:43:01,825
You hear me!

448
00:43:01,855 --> 00:43:03,855
So, you fooled me!

449
00:43:04,365 --> 00:43:06,395
So, you deceived me!

450
00:43:06,545 --> 00:43:08,415
So, you deceived me!

451
00:43:08,455 --> 00:43:10,455
You're done.

452
00:43:11,455 --> 00:43:13,025
Don't run away, man!

453
00:43:13,145 --> 00:43:15,155
Come here, don't run, Cerguday, I'll
tear you apart!

454
00:43:15,225 --> 00:43:17,225
- Come here!
- Ülgen Hatun!

455
00:43:17,315 --> 00:43:19,055
May your conquest be good, my Bey.

456
00:43:20,635 --> 00:43:23,035
Thank you, Malhun.

457
00:43:23,415 --> 00:43:26,515
Marmaracık has brought us
one step closer to our goal.

458
00:43:26,575 --> 00:43:28,575
Thanks to you, we got closer, Osman.

459
00:43:29,755 --> 00:43:33,455
You run towards your goal without
resting or stopping for a moment.

460
00:43:35,325 --> 00:43:37,335
And you work very hard too.

461
00:43:37,545 --> 00:43:39,675
Tell me, how are the boys?

462
00:43:40,215 --> 00:43:43,435
I sent Orhan and Alaaddin
to Karacahisar.

463
00:43:43,615 --> 00:43:46,375
Fatma and Halime are in the palace
with the ladies.

464
00:43:47,215 --> 00:43:49,375
What are the conditions in Yenişehir?

465
00:43:49,485 --> 00:43:52,285
That woman called Frigg, is
there any word on her?

466
00:43:53,195 --> 00:43:55,055
None yet.

467
00:43:55,085 --> 00:43:58,205
But the fall of her mask is near.

468
00:44:00,015 --> 00:44:01,585
Inshallah.

469
00:44:02,315 --> 00:44:04,115
This will also happen, Inshallah.

470
00:44:06,095 --> 00:44:07,445
My Beyç

471
00:44:07,575 --> 00:44:09,595
To whom will you give Marmaracık?

472
00:44:09,675 --> 00:44:11,675
Do you have a name in mind?

473
00:44:18,255 --> 00:44:20,075
Won't you tell me too, Osman?

474
00:44:22,175 --> 00:44:24,665
Everyone will know when
the time is right, Malhun.

475
00:44:32,285 --> 00:44:35,215
Konya / Seljuqs Palace

476
00:45:08,175 --> 00:45:10,245
Will you let me in, Sultan?

477
00:45:10,255 --> 00:45:12,145
Come in.

478
00:45:20,345 --> 00:45:22,095
Valide Sultan.

479
00:45:22,125 --> 00:45:25,625
Bayındır Bey has sent a
word from Yenişehir.

480
00:45:26,795 --> 00:45:28,095
Read it.

481
00:45:28,095 --> 00:45:30,095
What did he write?

482
00:45:35,305 --> 00:45:38,475
The sun of Seljuqs', Valide Sultan.

483
00:45:44,345 --> 00:45:45,715
Read.

484
00:45:51,305 --> 00:45:53,815
Osman Bey has outgrown
the post of sovereign.

485
00:45:54,875 --> 00:45:58,945
He
became a threat to the unity of the state.

486
00:45:59,545 --> 00:46:03,565
He interfered in the
internal affairs of Constantinople.

487
00:46:04,225 --> 00:46:08,775
It caused us many
calamities and caused us pain.

488
00:46:24,805 --> 00:46:27,295
Not only that, but the conquests...

489
00:46:27,355 --> 00:46:28,905
He gets stronger day by day.

490
00:46:28,935 --> 00:46:34,735
He is about to take power at the borders
from the mighty Seljuk state.

491
00:46:42,155 --> 00:46:45,075
My Sultan, who makes the world
tremble in fear of her power...

492
00:46:46,245 --> 00:46:52,575
Come and see and crush those
who doubt your strength.

493
00:46:54,425 --> 00:46:57,445
Your helpless man, Bayındır.

494
00:47:09,995 --> 00:47:11,335
Pity!

495
00:47:16,375 --> 00:47:19,125
While we are here to fight for survival...

496
00:47:21,485 --> 00:47:24,375
Osman sees this as an opportunity
to take advantage of.

497
00:47:25,875 --> 00:47:27,235
Pity!

498
00:47:35,345 --> 00:47:37,615
We fed him with our own hands...

499
00:47:39,045 --> 00:47:40,845
If he betrayed...

500
00:47:43,715 --> 00:47:47,545
his end is known.

501
00:48:01,605 --> 00:48:03,665
Whom we fed with our own hands...

502
00:48:04,635 --> 00:48:07,795
We trample it with our feet.

503
00:48:18,855 --> 00:48:20,605
I possess this power.

504
00:48:22,265 --> 00:48:24,415
I will not hesitate to use it.

505
00:48:29,665 --> 00:48:30,995
Avcı.

506
00:48:33,135 --> 00:48:35,205
Equip your most skilled warriors.

507
00:48:35,955 --> 00:48:37,815
We will go to Yenişehir.

508
00:48:38,475 --> 00:48:40,345
What shall we do, my Sultan?

509
00:48:45,255 --> 00:48:47,135
We will eliminate the disobedient.

510
00:48:48,455 --> 00:48:51,505
Either they kneel down and
tell us their loyalty to us...

511
00:48:52,185 --> 00:49:00,715
or they will meet the same fate
as my beloved bird.

512
00:49:02,535 --> 00:49:05,035
Marmaracık Castle

513
00:49:22,085 --> 00:49:24,475
Attention, Osman Bey!

514
00:49:24,635 --> 00:49:27,995
In the name of Allah.

515
00:49:48,885 --> 00:49:50,235
Salam Alaikum.

516
00:49:50,275 --> 00:49:52,115
Alaikum Salam.

517
00:49:52,715 --> 00:49:54,485
Good evening.

518
00:50:02,835 --> 00:50:07,945
Marmaracık Castle is not
just a property for us.

519
00:50:08,135 --> 00:50:12,815
Rather, it was the home of those who want
to spread sedition in our lands.

520
00:50:15,245 --> 00:50:18,875
But we got rid of them all.

521
00:50:22,825 --> 00:50:27,885
For this reason, we serve
our feast in our land.

522
00:50:29,185 --> 00:50:32,225
Thank Allah who has blessed
us with the vision of these days.

523
00:50:32,245 --> 00:50:34,295
Amin.

524
00:50:36,175 --> 00:50:37,595
Go ahead.

525
00:50:50,885 --> 00:50:53,215
Congratulations on your
new land, Osman Bey.

526
00:50:58,935 --> 00:51:01,005
But we are upset.

527
00:51:05,725 --> 00:51:11,775
We wanted to be with you
in a conquest like this.

528
00:51:12,975 --> 00:51:14,485
Öktem Bey.

529
00:51:16,835 --> 00:51:19,145
There is a secret to every conquest.

530
00:51:22,095 --> 00:51:27,435
Sometimes this mystery
is the key to this conquest.

531
00:51:29,915 --> 00:51:31,285
Yes.

532
00:51:36,815 --> 00:51:38,325
Beys.

533
00:51:39,835 --> 00:51:43,525
Don't be upset because I didn't
invite you to this conquest.

534
00:51:45,215 --> 00:51:47,375
We will have many conquests.

535
00:51:48,355 --> 00:51:53,575
Even if not today, we will kill
all of the infidels tomorrow.

536
00:51:56,145 --> 00:51:58,805
We will always carry our flag
together.

537
00:51:58,805 --> 00:52:00,335
Inshallah.

538
00:52:00,925 --> 00:52:01,985
Inshallah.

539
00:52:03,335 --> 00:52:04,585
May Allah bless you.

540
00:52:07,095 --> 00:52:09,255
Isn't that right, Kantakuzenos?

541
00:52:10,515 --> 00:52:14,075
How are you? Do they host you well?

542
00:52:14,295 --> 00:52:15,835
As you said, Osman Bey.

543
00:52:16,715 --> 00:52:20,285
I will hold you accountable
for what you did to me.

544
00:52:21,255 --> 00:52:24,315
If not today, then tomorrow.

545
00:52:24,945 --> 00:52:27,125
You put poison in
Kantakuzenos' food, right?

546
00:52:36,205 --> 00:52:38,365
Enjoy, Prince.

547
00:52:38,895 --> 00:52:40,055
Eat your food.

548
00:52:41,525 --> 00:52:43,035
I know.

549
00:52:44,165 --> 00:52:46,905
But I know how to take revenge too.

550
00:52:48,535 --> 00:52:51,145
You say we won't stop, right, Osman Bey?

551
00:52:51,245 --> 00:52:54,795
We will not stop. It
is not worthy of us, Öktem Bey.

552
00:52:55,705 --> 00:52:58,205
We will continue with the conquests.

553
00:52:58,265 --> 00:52:59,485
Good.

554
00:52:59,555 --> 00:53:01,685
Our hearts have now rejoiced, Osman Bey.

555
00:53:01,905 --> 00:53:04,095
Yes.

556
00:53:06,925 --> 00:53:09,775
What a secretive woman
you are, Malhun Hatun.

557
00:53:10,495 --> 00:53:14,445
I came and asked, but you said nothing.

558
00:53:15,545 --> 00:53:17,435
But I'm a little upset.

559
00:53:18,885 --> 00:53:22,625
Are we enemies?
Why all this mystery?

560
00:53:23,525 --> 00:53:25,255
No, Bengi Hatun.

561
00:53:25,795 --> 00:53:27,885
The state secret can not be said.

562
00:53:28,645 --> 00:53:31,235
Our action is not only towards you.

563
00:53:35,775 --> 00:53:36,865
Bala Hatun.

564
00:53:38,085 --> 00:53:40,135
You were in the conquest too, right?

565
00:53:40,225 --> 00:53:41,305
Yes.

566
00:53:42,785 --> 00:53:44,795
Mashallah, Bala Hatun.

567
00:53:45,035 --> 00:53:49,275
You don't stop even for a moment and run
after your husband from war to war.

568
00:53:49,625 --> 00:53:51,985
We hear your victories
and we are proud of you.

569
00:53:52,115 --> 00:53:53,465
Thank you.

570
00:53:53,905 --> 00:53:56,855
Not our victory, but the
victory of the sisters.

571
00:53:59,655 --> 00:54:00,985
Alçiçek.

572
00:54:01,805 --> 00:54:03,815
Come to our rehearsals someday.

573
00:54:05,115 --> 00:54:07,335
I would very much
like it, Bala Hatun.

574
00:54:18,525 --> 00:54:20,075
Salam Alaikum.

575
00:54:20,185 --> 00:54:22,425
Alaikum Salam.

576
00:54:23,175 --> 00:54:24,685
CongratulationsEnjoy your food.

577
00:54:32,375 --> 00:54:34,445
Welcome, my Sheikh.

578
00:54:34,605 --> 00:54:36,605
Thank you, Osman Bey.

579
00:54:37,895 --> 00:54:40,795
May Allah bless your conquest, Osman Bey.

580
00:54:40,985 --> 00:54:42,855
Thank you.

581
00:54:48,975 --> 00:54:52,585
O Allah, the owner of the lands...

582
00:54:53,185 --> 00:54:55,885
You give the property
(land) to whom you will...

583
00:54:56,395 --> 00:54:59,125
you take it from whomever you want.

584
00:55:01,925 --> 00:55:08,175
You praise whom you will and
humiliate whom You will.

585
00:55:08,405 --> 00:55:17,445
You have power over all things.

586
00:55:18,155 --> 00:55:23,185
Oh Allah, praise the dearest heroes
who fight for you.

587
00:55:23,255 --> 00:55:24,565
Amin.

588
00:55:24,725 --> 00:55:29,725
Make us victorious
in this blessed case.

589
00:55:29,745 --> 00:55:31,825
Amin.

590
00:55:45,535 --> 00:55:47,005
Go ahead, my Sheikh, go ahead.

591
00:55:47,045 --> 00:55:48,425
Thank you.

592
00:55:50,705 --> 00:55:52,705
In the name of of Allah the Merciful.

593
00:55:54,905 --> 00:55:57,575
In the name of of Allah the Merciful.

594
00:56:05,575 --> 00:56:07,115
Osman Bey.

595
00:56:08,085 --> 00:56:11,315
A land who has no owner is like a
flag without wind.

596
00:56:11,855 --> 00:56:15,185
Will you not say to whom
you will give judgment?

597
00:56:22,495 --> 00:56:23,855
I will say.

598
00:56:25,445 --> 00:56:27,005
I will definitely say.

599
00:56:32,655 --> 00:56:39,175
But I will reveal the owner tomorrow.

600
00:56:44,335 --> 00:56:47,175
Come on, enjoy your food.

601
00:56:49,465 --> 00:56:51,535
In the name of of Allah the Merciful.

602
00:56:53,285 --> 00:56:55,335
In the name of of Allah the Merciful.

603
00:56:56,175 --> 00:56:57,525
Thank you.

604
00:57:55,365 --> 00:57:58,425
Like our sword and shield, however...

605
00:58:10,135 --> 00:58:13,825
Look at the movements.

606
00:58:13,835 --> 00:58:16,725
O Allah.

607
00:58:44,795 --> 00:58:46,095
Eat.

608
00:58:46,885 --> 00:58:48,435
Thanks.

609
00:58:49,505 --> 00:58:52,415
We do not eat animals that are slaughtered
without Basmala.

610
00:58:52,895 --> 00:58:54,435
As you like.

611
00:58:54,835 --> 00:58:56,405
We eat it.

612
00:58:56,415 --> 00:58:57,965
Enjoy it.

613
00:59:11,095 --> 00:59:12,915
You made the right decision.

614
00:59:14,565 --> 00:59:16,105
If we unite...

615
00:59:16,775 --> 00:59:18,665
We will end Osman.

616
00:59:20,205 --> 00:59:22,755
I am not a man who works with infidels.

617
00:59:23,785 --> 00:59:25,785
I don't love you very much.

618
00:59:26,595 --> 00:59:27,925
You should know.

619
00:59:28,345 --> 00:59:31,665
However, Osman Bey disappointed me a lot.

620
00:59:33,135 --> 00:59:35,175
He did me wrong.

621
00:59:35,195 --> 00:59:37,515
He did not succeed in
keeping me by his side...

622
00:59:38,075 --> 00:59:41,145
even though I sacrificed myself for him.

623
00:59:43,145 --> 00:59:44,365
I...

624
00:59:44,965 --> 00:59:47,785
I have no choice but to agree with you.

625
00:59:48,735 --> 00:59:50,435
Osman was wrong.

626
00:59:51,025 --> 00:59:53,195
He thought the real Vizier was a puppet.

627
00:59:53,385 --> 00:59:55,895
But when you unite with
us and bring him down...

628
00:59:56,915 --> 00:59:58,415
He will face the bitter truth.

629
00:59:58,905 --> 01:00:02,695
He will face it, he will face it.

630
01:00:03,255 --> 01:00:06,025
He will pay for his betrayal...

631
01:00:06,345 --> 01:00:09,725
when he wakes up from
the dream of the state.

632
01:00:11,225 --> 01:00:13,725
Never forget what Osman did to you.

633
01:00:14,795 --> 01:00:16,525
Keep your anger burning.

634
01:00:16,705 --> 01:00:18,295
So that...

635
01:00:19,445 --> 01:00:23,495
when you destroy Osman, you will need it.

636
01:00:23,975 --> 01:00:26,215
Don't worry about that.

637
01:00:27,425 --> 01:00:29,225
I keep any promise I make.

638
01:00:31,345 --> 01:00:34,045
We will get along well, Olof.

639
01:00:34,875 --> 01:00:38,105
We will get along well.

640
01:01:05,745 --> 01:01:08,035
- Give me the sherbet, Ülgen Hatun.
- Wait, girl.

641
01:01:08,055 --> 01:01:10,075
Keep my mother busy.

642
01:01:10,375 --> 01:01:11,495
What do you say, girl?

643
01:01:11,515 --> 01:01:14,025
Your mother will eat
my flesh raw, Alçiçek!

644
01:01:21,255 --> 01:01:22,955
Have a drink, Subasi.

645
01:01:23,695 --> 01:01:25,235
Alçiçek.

646
01:01:25,275 --> 01:01:27,335
Don't get up, my mother will see you.

647
01:01:47,275 --> 01:01:50,285
Go to Güneştepe tomorrow morning.

648
01:01:50,665 --> 01:01:53,005
Let's meet at the tree
where we rode horses.

649
01:01:55,425 --> 01:01:57,425
- What do you mean?
- Drink sherbet.

650
01:02:05,165 --> 01:02:06,675
Bengi Hatun.

651
01:02:07,125 --> 01:02:09,075
You are a very
beautiful lady, Mashallah!

652
01:02:09,095 --> 01:02:11,095
Of course, Alçiçek resembles your beauty.

653
01:02:12,585 --> 01:02:14,875
Don't forget, I will wait for you.

654
01:02:17,105 --> 01:02:18,935
My eyes were dazzled.

655
01:02:19,105 --> 01:02:22,125
How bright you are tonight
like the moon, Mashallah!

656
01:02:23,025 --> 01:02:24,555
Ülgen Hatun.

657
01:02:25,655 --> 01:02:26,975
Stay away

658
01:03:23,835 --> 01:03:25,345
Alps!

659
01:03:27,485 --> 01:03:29,185
Draw your swords.

660
01:03:31,005 --> 01:03:32,525
Your command, my Bey.

661
01:03:32,545 --> 01:03:33,565
Your command, my Bey.

662
01:03:33,585 --> 01:03:35,155
Come on, brothers.

663
01:03:35,285 --> 01:03:36,595
Let's go

664
01:03:54,045 --> 01:03:55,635
Mashallah!

665
01:04:17,405 --> 01:04:19,135
Mashallah!

666
01:06:23,135 --> 01:06:24,635
Mashallah!

667
01:06:26,135 --> 01:06:27,915
May Allah protect you, valiants.

668
01:06:58,365 --> 01:06:59,925
O, throne...

669
01:07:04,435 --> 01:07:05,805
Tell me.

670
01:07:08,035 --> 01:07:10,035
How many valiants did you have?

671
01:07:12,705 --> 01:07:14,015
Tell me.

672
01:07:19,395 --> 01:07:21,925
How many families
have been broken?

673
01:07:34,765 --> 01:07:36,285
O, throne...

674
01:08:01,215 --> 01:08:02,725
Oh Throne!

675
01:08:05,705 --> 01:08:07,015
Speak!

676
01:08:09,055 --> 01:08:10,405
Speak!

677
01:08:12,175 --> 01:08:13,555
Speak!

678
01:08:29,995 --> 01:08:31,314
Speak!

679
01:08:43,625 --> 01:08:45,854
How many countries have you sent to hell?

680
01:08:55,085 --> 01:08:57,225
How many countries have you sent to hell?

681
01:09:04,585 --> 01:09:06,325
Do not approach me.

682
01:09:08,145 --> 01:09:09,925
Don't ever come out in front of me.

683
01:09:11,444 --> 01:09:13,774
Don't let me fall into your trap.

684
01:09:15,725 --> 01:09:17,314
Don't, or else...

685
01:09:23,015 --> 01:09:25,055
I told you not to let anyone in!

686
01:09:29,965 --> 01:09:32,705
Has the throne troubled you already, Osman?

687
01:10:08,405 --> 01:10:09,755
I'm afraid.

688
01:10:10,225 --> 01:10:11,995
I am afraid, my sheikh.

689
01:10:12,355 --> 01:10:14,085
I am very afraid.

690
01:10:17,665 --> 01:10:19,495
You should be afraid.

691
01:10:20,625 --> 01:10:24,705
If I were a Bey,
I would also be very afraid.

692
01:10:25,185 --> 01:10:29,975
I would be frightened.

693
01:10:38,985 --> 01:10:43,535
If this throne becomes a grave for me,
I'll destroy it!

694
01:10:45,225 --> 01:10:49,865
You need to control yourself first.

695
01:10:50,305 --> 01:10:52,015
You are now a Bey.

696
01:10:53,145 --> 01:10:56,645
You are now the ruler of many
souls and many Beys.

697
01:10:57,155 --> 01:11:00,735
You are the Bey of alps and merchants.

698
01:11:01,655 --> 01:11:03,705
You ruled your soul.

699
01:11:05,305 --> 01:11:08,115
What about the souls of your people?

700
01:11:09,325 --> 01:11:13,855
What about your men's endless desires ?

701
01:11:17,365 --> 01:11:18,935
They will ask for booty.

702
01:11:20,215 --> 01:11:22,315
They will ask for positions and ranks.

703
01:11:22,795 --> 01:11:28,855
They will ask for supplies, they will ask
for order, they will ask for tranquility

704
01:11:30,225 --> 01:11:33,705
...they will ask and they will ask.

705
01:11:33,885 --> 01:11:36,355
If you provide, you are great.

706
01:11:38,255 --> 01:11:39,905
And if you don't provide...

707
01:11:41,705 --> 01:11:47,515
If I don't provide, I'll be the worst
in their eyes.

708
01:11:49,465 --> 01:11:55,495
This is why a Bey is always lonely.

709
01:11:55,905 --> 01:11:59,885
You look from the outside
and you see a lot of servants around.

710
01:12:00,585 --> 01:12:04,145
However, the one who is willing to lead...

711
01:12:04,895 --> 01:12:09,505
...should also accept being alone.

712
01:12:10,625 --> 01:12:12,685
What does loneliness mean, my sheik?

713
01:12:13,655 --> 01:12:15,215
What is loneliness?

714
01:12:15,415 --> 01:12:18,495
Those who would sacrifice
their lives for you....

715
01:12:18,495 --> 01:12:22,245
...might be your worst enemy someday.

716
01:12:22,765 --> 01:12:26,525
Your wife, with whom you rest your head
on the same pillow...

717
01:12:26,525 --> 01:12:28,845
might make an alliance with your enemy.

718
01:12:28,845 --> 01:12:30,915
Your children who you care about so much...

719
01:12:31,515 --> 01:12:37,575
...might face you on a battlefield
to take the throne.

720
01:12:38,385 --> 01:12:42,645
And a lot more to come, my Osman.

721
01:12:45,225 --> 01:12:47,075
What is the cure of this, my Bey?

722
01:12:48,145 --> 01:12:50,545
The demon that bothers a Bey is huge.

723
01:12:51,625 --> 01:12:56,665
You must be vigilant to get rid
of this eternal enemy.

724
01:13:05,055 --> 01:13:06,555
How can I?

725
01:13:11,135 --> 01:13:13,145
You should always be on alert.

726
01:13:13,145 --> 01:13:16,905
How can I always be on alert, my sheik?

727
01:13:18,675 --> 01:13:20,545
By opening the eyes of your heart.

728
01:13:22,235 --> 01:13:23,695
How do I do it?

729
01:13:25,405 --> 01:13:30,145
You will spend your nights
thinking and remembering your Creator.

730
01:13:31,765 --> 01:13:33,845
Morning prayer is not enough.

731
01:13:35,165 --> 01:13:40,005
You will pray Tahajjud and
fast the Sunnahs.

732
01:13:40,005 --> 01:13:46,645
While everyone donates one,
you'll donate a thousand.

733
01:13:49,845 --> 01:13:54,625
You will erase the life in world
from your heart and throw it away.

734
01:13:54,765 --> 01:13:57,835
You will preserve monotheism in your heart.

735
01:13:57,835 --> 01:14:07,355
If you illuminate your night and day by reading
the Holy Quran, you will remain awake.

736
01:14:07,585 --> 01:14:11,665
The eyes of your heart open when you stay awake.

737
01:14:12,945 --> 01:14:15,225
Whenever the eyes of your heart opens...

738
01:14:16,145 --> 01:14:20,650
You will see the abundance of Allah...

739
01:14:20,650 --> 01:14:26,150
...manifesting Himself upon you when you
speak, when you see, and when you think

740
01:14:27,965 --> 01:14:33,945
And your followers who will see
your situation will straighten up little by little

741
01:14:36,815 --> 01:14:43,125
But every rose has a thorn, Bey Osman.

742
01:14:43,485 --> 01:14:44,805
Valiant Osman.

743
01:14:45,885 --> 01:14:48,535
And that will be your test.

744
01:14:49,065 --> 01:14:53,965
What's important here is to
pass that test.

745
01:14:54,365 --> 01:14:58,025
May Allah help us pass
the tests on earth, my sheik.

746
01:15:00,105 --> 01:15:03,075
- Amen.
- Amen.

747
01:15:12,395 --> 01:15:14,955
Yeni Sehir

748
01:15:22,095 --> 01:15:28,475
Praise be!
Praise be!

749
01:15:33,385 --> 01:15:38,445
My Bey, that Olof seems spook,
I don't know.

750
01:15:44,665 --> 01:15:48,405
Are you questioning my judgment
with your sparrow-sized brain?

751
01:15:48,835 --> 01:15:50,205
Not at all, my Bey.

752
01:15:50,455 --> 01:15:52,735
I am just trying to keep
danger away from you.

753
01:15:52,735 --> 01:15:55,385
The danger comes from Osman.

754
01:15:55,935 --> 01:15:57,155
Marmar....

755
01:15:57,775 --> 01:16:02,255
At the Marmaracik siege, I risked my life!

756
01:16:03,575 --> 01:16:07,155
Forget my life!
I risked my wealth!

757
01:16:08,035 --> 01:16:09,155
What did Osman do?

758
01:16:09,715 --> 01:16:12,345
He put that hairy Turgut
upon us!

759
01:16:13,485 --> 01:16:15,315
You know the right thing, my Bey.

760
01:16:15,455 --> 01:16:17,935
I know, I know of course.

761
01:16:19,835 --> 01:16:25,645
When it's about the battle,
let's call Bayindir!

762
01:16:26,085 --> 01:16:31,155
When the battle is over, when the council
meets, go off Bayindir! Go check your stall!

763
01:16:33,155 --> 01:16:39,555
No surprise an arrognat like Osman
has such an ingratitude.

764
01:16:40,075 --> 01:16:44,125
I know what to do.

765
01:16:44,765 --> 01:16:47,475
I'll wipe them all out, all of them.

766
01:16:48,135 --> 01:16:51,885
From Osman to Turgut, to Oktem.

767
01:16:52,835 --> 01:16:54,595
I am united with Olof now.

768
01:16:56,035 --> 01:16:58,525
I will do what he asks.

769
01:16:59,065 --> 01:17:02,735
And he will build a ladder out of his golds
for me.

770
01:17:03,595 --> 01:17:07,935
And with that ladder
I will hit Osman's head!

771
01:17:12,035 --> 01:17:14,505
He used Bayindir and conquered the castle.

772
01:17:14,975 --> 01:17:17,325
Yet he didn't invite Bayindir to the council.

773
01:17:19,925 --> 01:17:22,445
Consider this as an example, Bey.

774
01:17:23,945 --> 01:17:25,735
I see, Hatun.

775
01:17:27,585 --> 01:17:29,315
I see, but I don't understand.

776
01:17:29,975 --> 01:17:32,935
Why doesn't he invite Bayindir
but us?

777
01:17:33,435 --> 01:17:36,535
He took the castle and finished his job
with Bayindir.

778
01:17:36,935 --> 01:17:42,115
He's now showing off to you and the
other Beys.

779
01:17:44,375 --> 01:17:46,515
Let's see to whom he'll give the castle.

780
01:17:49,865 --> 01:17:56,785
Marmaragic stretches like
a hammerhead on the path of our conquest.

781
01:17:56,785 --> 01:17:58,595
Thank Allah.

782
01:17:59,395 --> 01:18:01,235
If we do not take measures...

783
01:18:02,525 --> 01:18:04,435
...they will carve out this place
and take it from us

784
01:18:05,315 --> 01:18:06,945
What's the measure, Osman Bey?

785
01:18:07,335 --> 01:18:08,705
We won't stop.

786
01:18:11,345 --> 01:18:16,285
If we stop, that is going to be a
free offer for them.

787
01:18:16,325 --> 01:18:18,005
But if we move on...

788
01:18:19,115 --> 01:18:24,775
...we will then face their attacks
with our hardened hearts

789
01:18:26,605 --> 01:18:28,405
We'll take Kopruhisar.

790
01:18:29,895 --> 01:18:34,965
My Bey, don't we need to wait a bit?
They must be on alert now.

791
01:18:36,825 --> 01:18:38,435
This is how they think.

792
01:18:39,925 --> 01:18:42,915
Just like how we pushed Inegol
after conquering Bilecik...

793
01:18:43,625 --> 01:18:48,585
They think we'll push Kopruhisar after
Marmaracik.

794
01:18:49,775 --> 01:18:53,875
They gather soldiers from the villages,
fortify the walls.

795
01:18:53,985 --> 01:18:55,875
What is your move, Osman Bey?

796
01:18:56,085 --> 01:19:00,755
We will pretend that we have stopped, but
we will continue our preparations in secret.

797
01:19:01,805 --> 01:19:04,715
When they think we won't move...

798
01:19:05,655 --> 01:19:08,155
...we will hit them
when they're unprepared.

799
01:19:10,645 --> 01:19:13,655
...but still, it
won't be as easy as Marmaragic.

800
01:19:14,575 --> 01:19:16,805
It has never been easy, my Bey.

801
01:19:19,075 --> 01:19:22,925
Call Beys,
I will announce the ruler of Marmaragic.

802
01:19:27,955 --> 01:19:31,585
After that, we will start
preparations for the siege quickly.

803
01:19:41,335 --> 01:19:43,495
- Boran.
- My Bey.

804
01:19:47,065 --> 01:19:50,295
- Call commander Remus.
- Command is yours, my Bey.

805
01:19:55,325 --> 01:19:57,435
If he had invited us to the war...

806
01:19:59,435 --> 01:20:05,795
I would have hoped he'd give it to us.

807
01:20:06,165 --> 01:20:13,745
But it seems like
Turgut Bey will rule the castle.

808
01:20:14,475 --> 01:20:16,415
For this reason, he does not invite you.

809
01:20:16,995 --> 01:20:19,205
It is you who deserves the castle!

810
01:20:19,485 --> 01:20:23,315
If you had participated in the conquest,
he would be obliged to give it to you.

811
01:20:23,315 --> 01:20:25,695
But now he will give it to Turgut Bey.

812
01:20:29,235 --> 01:20:33,425
You're right,
you are always right...

813
01:20:34,775 --> 01:20:36,605
...but I just can't accept.

814
01:20:37,505 --> 01:20:42,915
If you had listened to me, you would be the
Bey of the district now, not Osman Bey.

815
01:20:45,775 --> 01:20:48,855
Anyway, we'll be late for the meeting.

816
01:20:49,375 --> 01:20:50,745
Let's go.

817
01:20:54,445 --> 01:20:56,455
Is Alcicek not going to the market?

818
01:20:57,205 --> 01:21:01,035
She has things to do in the tent.
She'll go when she's finished.

819
01:21:01,845 --> 01:21:03,235
Okay.

820
01:21:05,235 --> 01:21:08,295
Bayindir Bey, are you inside?

821
01:21:14,415 --> 01:21:15,775
Yes, Samil alp?

822
01:21:16,675 --> 01:21:20,035
- Peace be upon you
- Peace be upon you.

823
01:21:20,535 --> 01:21:22,235
What's it, Samil Alp?

824
01:21:22,265 --> 01:21:26,725
Osman Bey is conducting a meeting.
He invites all the Beys.

825
01:21:28,295 --> 01:21:31,575
Our Bey's invitatiton is a command for us.

826
01:21:31,955 --> 01:21:33,495
You shall go.

827
01:21:33,555 --> 01:21:37,065
We will be there before everyone else,
Insha Allah.

828
01:21:40,245 --> 01:21:42,585
Why are you closing the shop at this time?

829
01:21:43,485 --> 01:21:46,685
Samil Alp, you're inside the shop!

830
01:21:47,075 --> 01:21:49,675
The shop is open, not closed.

831
01:21:51,675 --> 01:21:52,755
Right.

832
01:22:07,555 --> 01:22:08,885
I saw the truth.

833
01:22:10,195 --> 01:22:14,395
And I saw how the heads of those who stood
against to the truth fell down.

834
01:22:19,335 --> 01:22:20,925
Will I be able to trust you?

835
01:22:26,115 --> 01:22:27,885
If I hadn't trusted you...

836
01:22:29,795 --> 01:22:31,605
I would have cut your
head off a long time ago.

837
01:22:36,765 --> 01:22:39,255
You will now go to the Emperor.

838
01:22:39,935 --> 01:22:45,025
You will say that Kantakouzanos,
the only heir to the throne, is in my hands.

839
01:22:46,055 --> 01:22:48,975
I am grateful for your confidence in me,
Osman Bey.

840
01:22:49,955 --> 01:22:54,835
But if Kantakouzanos is
collaborating with Olof...

841
01:22:55,725 --> 01:22:58,605
His survival
is the last thing you want.

842
01:22:58,835 --> 01:23:03,245
I know so I'm
only sending you to report the news.

843
01:23:05,075 --> 01:23:06,895
You are loyal to the Emperor.

844
01:23:07,665 --> 01:23:11,765
If you stay here, he won't let
Kantakouzanos live.

845
01:23:12,475 --> 01:23:20,115
I hope the Emperor will not fall into the trap of
these traitors and continue the enmity.

846
01:23:22,505 --> 01:23:27,575
You are a good friend.

847
01:23:30,585 --> 01:23:32,145
You are an honorable commander.

848
01:23:34,995 --> 01:23:36,235
Your way shall be open.

849
01:23:47,995 --> 01:23:51,145
- Summon the Beys.
- As you command, my Bey.

850
01:23:55,805 --> 01:23:58,155
We can't leave Remus in Osman's hands.

851
01:23:58,685 --> 01:24:03,045
You will have eyes in Yenişehir,
Marmaragic and everywhere else!

852
01:24:03,165 --> 01:24:05,165
You will track him down.

853
01:24:07,845 --> 01:24:09,765
What does Osman want from Remus?

854
01:24:11,395 --> 01:24:16,195
That merchant will tell us.
Bayindir.

855
01:24:18,455 --> 01:24:23,555
We will know every step Osman takes
thanks to him.

856
01:24:28,645 --> 01:24:33,345
If we give Binder a lot of gold,
he'll keep working for us.

857
01:24:34,995 --> 01:24:40,275
We can sacrifice some gold
to kill Osman, my love.

858
01:24:41,095 --> 01:24:47,685
Besides, when our business with that
merchant is done, we will get our gold back

859
01:24:53,065 --> 01:24:55,315
- Peace be upon you
- Peace be upon you

860
01:24:55,315 --> 01:24:57,545
Peace be upon you

861
01:24:57,605 --> 01:25:00,925
Come, Gurbuz Alp, come.
You can eat here, please

862
01:25:00,925 --> 01:25:05,285
You impress me when you talk about food,
Baysungur.

863
01:25:07,895 --> 01:25:09,665
Go ahead, Brother Gurbuz.

864
01:25:10,435 --> 01:25:12,205
Food, food!

865
01:25:12,655 --> 01:25:15,725
There is no food, I mean there is,
but it is enough for only me.

866
01:25:16,625 --> 01:25:20,045
Cerkutay never has enough of food.
You'll get used to him.

867
01:25:20,275 --> 01:25:21,635
You will get used.

868
01:25:25,585 --> 01:25:27,435
Come, Sister Ulgen, come!

869
01:25:29,345 --> 01:25:32,105
Come, sister Ulgen, come,
Gurbuz Alp is very hungry!

870
01:25:35,125 --> 01:25:36,415
Thank your hands.

871
01:25:39,155 --> 01:25:41,375
- Ulgen...
- Enjoy it!

872
01:25:45,235 --> 01:25:46,375
Ulgen Hatun.

873
01:25:47,385 --> 01:25:50,055
Enjoy it, enjoy it.

874
01:25:51,395 --> 01:25:52,755
Enjoy.

875
01:25:54,775 --> 01:25:56,295
...I'm here, here I am.

876
01:25:58,405 --> 01:25:59,965
I do not hear.

877
01:26:04,705 --> 01:26:07,255
Eat, alps, eat!
Enjoy it!

878
01:26:07,635 --> 01:26:09,405
- Let me enjoy it.
- This is for you.

879
01:26:10,545 --> 01:26:12,255
Enjoy it.

880
01:26:12,645 --> 01:26:17,185
I'm hungry, Ulgen Hatun,
I am hungry.

881
01:26:18,505 --> 01:26:21,485
Good, give me, give me!

882
01:26:23,015 --> 01:26:26,685
What is this?
This, is not enough.

883
01:26:26,685 --> 01:26:30,535
Think about all the meals you have
eaten so far!

884
01:26:31,075 --> 01:26:34,915
Sister, give me more.
this is not even slightly enough to fill me.

885
01:26:34,915 --> 01:26:36,915
Oh my!

886
01:26:43,065 --> 01:26:44,815
Give me a little more.

887
01:26:46,055 --> 01:26:47,835
Eat, Cerkutay, eat

888
01:26:48,295 --> 01:26:51,485
When we go to Kopruhisar,
you'll miss the meals of Yeni Sehir.

889
01:26:52,165 --> 01:26:53,475
Look.

890
01:26:54,215 --> 01:26:57,145
Osman Bey will give you a mission
in Kopruhisar.

891
01:26:57,145 --> 01:26:57,955
Yes.

892
01:27:03,875 --> 01:27:08,155
I mean, It's hiccup.

893
01:27:16,145 --> 01:27:17,445
Enjoy it.

894
01:27:18,085 --> 01:27:20,785
We hurt Ulgen Hatun so much.

895
01:27:30,515 --> 01:27:32,665
- Leave it.
- You leave it!

896
01:27:35,005 --> 01:27:38,135
You said your strength comes from
your heart.

897
01:27:38,785 --> 01:27:41,505
Of course you are strong after eating
all that food!

898
01:27:41,505 --> 01:27:43,505
Eat less!

899
01:27:43,505 --> 01:27:45,765
Leave it.

900
01:27:46,655 --> 01:27:48,185
You leave it.

901
01:27:48,385 --> 01:27:53,035
Brothers, look,
there is enough food for all of us.

902
01:27:55,155 --> 01:27:58,955
Come on, come on, eat your food quickly,
the meeting will be held soon.

903
01:27:58,955 --> 01:28:00,655
Come on, Cerkutay.

904
01:28:00,655 --> 01:28:02,655
How about sharing a bit of your food?

905
01:28:03,005 --> 01:28:04,535
Leave it!

906
01:28:19,485 --> 01:28:21,555
What Kopruhisar are they talking about?!

907
01:28:22,505 --> 01:28:24,385
Where on earth did this come from now?

908
01:28:25,135 --> 01:28:26,835
Oh how unlucky I am!

909
01:28:31,985 --> 01:28:33,355
My Bey.

910
01:28:39,305 --> 01:28:40,685
My Bey.

911
01:28:40,705 --> 01:28:43,705
The meeting is at the top,
why do we go down?

912
01:28:43,705 --> 01:28:47,705
If the meeting is upstairs,
why do you follow me?

913
01:28:47,805 --> 01:28:49,385
Shut up, okay!

914
01:28:49,535 --> 01:28:51,085
Wait here.

915
01:28:51,285 --> 01:28:52,805
Don't follow me.

916
01:29:14,085 --> 01:29:16,585
What's going on, Ulgen Hatun?
You are crying.

917
01:29:16,585 --> 01:29:18,585
What can it be?
Cerkutay!

918
01:29:19,055 --> 01:29:21,785
Ah, I mean Osman Bey!

919
01:29:22,335 --> 01:29:26,085
He will conquer Kopruhisar now.

920
01:29:27,685 --> 01:29:30,005
How beautiful!
What's the matter?

921
01:29:30,005 --> 01:29:32,005
There is definitely nothing wrong about it.

922
01:29:33,085 --> 01:29:34,635
Turks' land is expanding.

923
01:29:35,935 --> 01:29:44,455
Osman Bey will give Cerkutay a mission
on Kopruhisar.

924
01:29:45,835 --> 01:29:47,885
And this palace will lose its joy.

925
01:29:50,205 --> 01:29:52,005
I don't say it for myself.

926
01:29:53,255 --> 01:29:58,685
Who would eat all this food
if Cerkutay wasn't around?

927
01:29:59,405 --> 01:30:01,785
That's why.

928
01:30:04,885 --> 01:30:07,355
Osman Bey.

929
01:30:08,955 --> 01:30:14,135
I knew you wouldn't stop
but I didn't know your destination.

930
01:30:15,205 --> 01:30:17,435
I learned it now.

931
01:30:18,555 --> 01:30:19,935
Kopruhisar, huh?

932
01:30:31,955 --> 01:30:33,985
Is there anything wrong, Bayindir Bey?

933
01:30:34,635 --> 01:30:36,435
The meeting is not in this way.

934
01:30:36,435 --> 01:30:38,235
Indeed, it isn't.

935
01:30:38,235 --> 01:30:41,985
Osman Bey builded such a huge palace that...

936
01:30:41,985 --> 01:30:45,535
...it's confusing the find your way to
the restroom.

937
01:30:45,805 --> 01:30:49,305
Tell me, my brothers, where is the meeting?

938
01:30:49,505 --> 01:30:51,505
The meeting is this way, Bayindir Bey.

939
01:30:51,505 --> 01:30:52,555
Let's go.

940
01:30:52,555 --> 01:30:54,555
Thank you, brothers.

941
01:31:06,685 --> 01:31:09,055
Osman Bey is moving to Kopruhisar.

942
01:31:09,635 --> 01:31:11,985
Go immediately to Olof and tell him.

943
01:31:24,955 --> 01:31:26,535
Attention!

944
01:31:26,705 --> 01:31:28,255
Osman Bey.

945
01:31:29,035 --> 01:31:31,085
May peace be upon you.

946
01:31:31,185 --> 01:31:33,735
And may peace be upon you.

947
01:31:46,985 --> 01:31:48,555
Please.

948
01:31:59,305 --> 01:32:04,530
The meeting shall begin
with the ninety-nine names of Allah,

949
01:32:04,530 --> 01:32:09,980
who considers us responsible
for the invasion, not for the victory

950
01:32:11,355 --> 01:32:15,635
In the name of of Allah the Merciful,
the Compassionate.

951
01:32:40,585 --> 01:32:42,435
Bayindir Bey

952
01:32:44,585 --> 01:32:49,955
When you first came, you brought a
chest of gold.

953
01:32:56,705 --> 01:32:58,285
Yes my Bey.

954
01:32:58,685 --> 01:33:01,255
This is correct.

955
01:33:04,855 --> 01:33:06,185
Bring it.

956
01:33:34,655 --> 01:33:40,105
This is your share of the booty
of the conquest of Marmaragic.

957
01:34:14,685 --> 01:34:16,405
May Allah bless you my Bey.

958
01:34:26,235 --> 01:34:31,785
This sword is a gift from me to you.

959
01:34:35,805 --> 01:34:37,335
May Allah bless you

960
01:34:45,435 --> 01:34:47,205
May Allah bless you, my Bey.

961
01:34:47,235 --> 01:34:52,105
I will always join you when you invite
me to a war.

962
01:34:53,435 --> 01:34:54,755
I'll always do.

963
01:34:57,235 --> 01:34:58,885
May Allah bless you my Bey.

964
01:35:14,955 --> 01:35:20,455
And now it is the turn of proclaiming the
ruler of Marmaragic.

965
01:35:29,385 --> 01:35:32,205
You all fought fiercely.

966
01:35:33,655 --> 01:35:37,485
And you watered the land of
the country with your blood and sweat

967
01:35:37,935 --> 01:35:39,655
Allah bless you.

968
01:35:43,235 --> 01:35:44,585
However...

969
01:35:47,185 --> 01:35:49,235
The one who paid the highest price...

970
01:35:51,485 --> 01:35:53,505
...shall rule Marmaragic.

971
01:35:58,085 --> 01:36:00,695
Of course, the price does not
mean everything.

972
01:36:01,335 --> 01:36:06,305
The origin of a man appears
in difficult days.

973
01:36:13,055 --> 01:36:18,655
Now I see that you are all
curious about what I am going to say.

974
01:36:19,585 --> 01:36:23,935
The name that will come out of my mouth
will not change anything for you.

975
01:36:25,955 --> 01:36:31,285
Our presence together is only to
carry our banner forward.

976
01:36:38,535 --> 01:36:43,835
...and for this reason,
the ruler of Marmaragic...

977
01:36:53,685 --> 01:36:55,405
...is Oktem Bey.

978
01:37:10,255 --> 01:37:11,755
Eyvallah my Bey.

979
01:37:13,255 --> 01:37:18,085
As long as you see me fit
for this sacred mission...

980
01:37:19,305 --> 01:37:21,105
Your relics are my relics.

981
01:37:22,235 --> 01:37:23,755
May Allah bless you

982
01:37:35,335 --> 01:37:37,455
Games have been played against you

983
01:37:37,635 --> 01:37:41,985
You raised your sword for the sake of your
name and the slander that befell your honor

984
01:37:42,685 --> 01:37:46,335
Nevertheless, you listened to your Bey.

985
01:37:48,185 --> 01:37:52,755
Marmaragic is your right
due to your attitude.

986
01:38:02,555 --> 01:38:04,305
I object.

987
01:38:31,825 --> 01:38:34,285
I have news from Bayindir Bey.

988
01:38:35,255 --> 01:38:36,485
Say it.

989
01:38:42,705 --> 01:38:44,255
I told you to speak!

990
01:38:45,455 --> 01:38:48,485
We've learned Osman Bey's next move.

991
01:38:49,185 --> 01:38:51,685
He will attack Kopruhisar.

992
01:39:07,435 --> 01:39:08,685
You were right.

993
01:39:09,835 --> 01:39:11,055
Osman won't stop.

994
01:39:12,105 --> 01:39:13,955
But now we know his move!

995
01:39:14,885 --> 01:39:17,155
Let's take him down since
he's in our hands, Olof

996
01:39:17,885 --> 01:39:19,155
We will

997
01:39:20,155 --> 01:39:22,705
But we have a job first.

998
01:39:24,055 --> 01:39:25,835
We'll catch Remus.

999
01:39:46,285 --> 01:39:47,635
Osman Bey.

1000
01:39:49,935 --> 01:39:55,685
We have offered many martyrs together
in many conquests.

1001
01:39:56,105 --> 01:39:58,235
Is only Oktem Bey having losses?

1002
01:39:58,235 --> 01:39:59,555
No.

1003
01:40:05,655 --> 01:40:07,755
You know my heart, Osman Bey.

1004
01:40:09,885 --> 01:40:12,535
I sacrificed everything I had for you.

1005
01:40:12,535 --> 01:40:16,835
My tribe, my alps, my Hatun.

1006
01:40:19,355 --> 01:40:21,405
If I had more, I would sacrifice it too.

1007
01:40:24,635 --> 01:40:27,005
I mean, my concern is not the throne.

1008
01:40:29,655 --> 01:40:31,145
However...

1009
01:40:33,885 --> 01:40:36,405
The throne of the land we conquered...

1010
01:40:38,305 --> 01:40:44,985
...belongs to a man who participated
in the war, who fought, who spilled blood.

1011
01:40:46,905 --> 01:40:51,935
How are we going to call people to fight
on our side if we act like this, Osman Bey?

1012
01:40:56,385 --> 01:40:58,555
We shall make new conquests, Turgut Bey.

1013
01:41:00,535 --> 01:41:06,635
Is what brings us together wealth?
Will we break when we don't have wealth?

1014
01:41:11,735 --> 01:41:13,505
Oktem Bey.

1015
01:41:15,235 --> 01:41:17,785
His nephew Batur became a martyr
for Marmaragic.

1016
01:41:21,285 --> 01:41:24,305
Even before he's pain eased off...
he was slandered

1017
01:41:28,185 --> 01:41:29,755
Therefore...

1018
01:41:36,135 --> 01:41:40,635
Marmaragic is his right because of the
pain he experienced.

1019
01:42:06,255 --> 01:42:07,955
The meeting is over.

1020
01:42:40,105 --> 01:42:41,635
Prepare the horses, Oktan.

1021
01:42:41,635 --> 01:42:43,635
Your command, my Bey.

1022
01:42:59,785 --> 01:43:01,305
Turgut Bey!

1023
01:43:12,585 --> 01:43:14,155
Yes, Turgut Bey.

1024
01:43:15,455 --> 01:43:18,705
...you have kicked us out
of Marmaragic, however...

1025
01:43:19,385 --> 01:43:22,885
...the throne is not left for us,
nor for you.

1026
01:43:23,705 --> 01:43:27,355
Why waste your breath on
nonsense, Bayindir Bey?

1027
01:43:27,355 --> 01:43:30,905
Are you trying to ignite discord?
Do I care about the throne?

1028
01:43:30,905 --> 01:43:32,905
Don't you care?

1029
01:43:33,255 --> 01:43:35,005
If you don't care it at all...

1030
01:43:35,955 --> 01:43:37,785
...why the long face?

1031
01:43:40,785 --> 01:43:45,985
Osman Bey thought
Oktam Bey has the right for the throne.

1032
01:43:46,235 --> 01:43:49,385
All we have to do is congratulate him.

1033
01:43:49,385 --> 01:43:50,905
Am I wrong?

1034
01:43:51,755 --> 01:43:56,585
What I should do is none of your business,
Bayindir Bey.

1035
01:43:58,985 --> 01:44:04,185
If you keep talking like this,
I won't mind the trouble.

1036
01:44:07,635 --> 01:44:09,205
Right.

1037
01:44:09,405 --> 01:44:11,005
We are in a Bey's mansion.

1038
01:44:12,305 --> 01:44:15,055
If we make a trouble right here...

1039
01:44:15,055 --> 01:44:17,055
People will say...

1040
01:44:18,005 --> 01:44:23,305
"Bayindir Bey couldn't accept Bayindir Bey
issue and created a trouble!"

1041
01:44:23,305 --> 01:44:25,985
Give me patience!

1042
01:44:25,985 --> 01:44:28,405
Yes, patience.

1043
01:44:28,405 --> 01:44:30,405
Patience.

1044
01:44:30,855 --> 01:44:32,705
Stay safe.

1045
01:44:39,985 --> 01:44:41,505
Oh patience!

1046
01:44:42,555 --> 01:44:44,105
Oh patience!

1047
01:44:47,125 --> 01:44:48,975
Come on Kutan, where are you?

1048
01:44:56,125 --> 01:44:57,865
Oh, Alcicek!

1049
01:44:58,005 --> 01:45:00,585
Where have you been?!

1050
01:45:00,665 --> 01:45:03,185
Come and I know what
I'm going to do to you!

1051
01:45:09,305 --> 01:45:12,535
- Congratulations my Bey!
- Eyvallah, eyvallah, thank you.

1052
01:45:13,325 --> 01:45:14,865
Thank you.

1053
01:45:22,105 --> 01:45:23,415
My Bey.

1054
01:45:23,925 --> 01:45:25,275
Hatun.

1055
01:45:26,485 --> 01:45:28,525
I hope you have good news, Inshallah.

1056
01:45:28,915 --> 01:45:30,985
It's good news.

1057
01:45:31,895 --> 01:45:34,985
You got very angry with Osman Bey...

1058
01:45:35,645 --> 01:45:37,995
but Osman Bey acted like a real Bey.

1059
01:45:39,365 --> 01:45:42,665
He thinks Marmaracik is our right.

1060
01:45:45,185 --> 01:45:47,655
Marmaracik is ours now, Hatun.

1061
01:45:48,625 --> 01:45:50,795
Oh my!

1062
01:45:51,105 --> 01:45:53,655
He wouldn't find someone better than you.

1063
01:45:58,145 --> 01:46:02,535
Even if he is late, Osman has found
the man who will have his back.

1064
01:46:03,395 --> 01:46:05,435
Eyvallah Hatun, Eyvallah.

1065
01:46:08,065 --> 01:46:12,935
I am not sure if they deceive us or not.

1066
01:46:14,685 --> 01:46:17,265
Why would they deceive us?

1067
01:46:20,985 --> 01:46:24,505
Osman's nephew.
Aktemur.

1068
01:46:33,545 --> 01:46:34,865
Tell me.

1069
01:46:37,445 --> 01:46:43,685
Hanging around our daughter, Alcicek.

1070
01:46:52,495 --> 01:46:54,065
Subasi.

1071
01:47:05,265 --> 01:47:08,365
I thought you were
going to say something bad, Hatun!

1072
01:47:08,675 --> 01:47:11,945
That's good news, good, Aktemur
is a good boy.

1073
01:47:12,405 --> 01:47:13,925
He is a good boy.

1074
01:47:14,235 --> 01:47:16,595
If something is going to happen,
let it happen.

1075
01:47:16,595 --> 01:47:18,105
Oktem Bey!

1076
01:47:19,055 --> 01:47:22,105
I'm telling you Aktemur
is a good boy, Hatun!

1077
01:47:22,235 --> 01:47:26,465
Also, can we find a better groom
than Osman Bey's nephew?

1078
01:47:31,995 --> 01:47:35,515
Does our daughter's heart
feel the same?

1079
01:48:18,585 --> 01:48:20,245
If I waited a little longer...

1080
01:48:20,325 --> 01:48:23,135
I would have been rooted in the ground like
this tree, Subasi.

1081
01:48:23,395 --> 01:48:27,185
Should I have hurried to talk to
a Hatun who is not in love with me?

1082
01:48:28,635 --> 01:48:30,535
If you don't want this at all...

1083
01:48:30,845 --> 01:48:33,205
You shouldn't have come!
Why did you come?

1084
01:48:36,405 --> 01:48:37,725
Give me patience.

1085
01:48:40,045 --> 01:48:42,085
Give me patience, Alcicek Hatun!

1086
01:48:43,175 --> 01:48:44,685
You called me!

1087
01:48:45,395 --> 01:48:47,145
You said it was important!

1088
01:48:49,045 --> 01:48:51,635
Apparently, you haven't had enough.

1089
01:48:52,255 --> 01:48:55,305
You wanted to call me here and
chew me out a bit more.

1090
01:48:56,655 --> 01:48:58,465
You knew I'd come.

1091
01:48:58,845 --> 01:49:00,375
You know I like you.

1092
01:49:01,275 --> 01:49:02,795
You knew I would.

1093
01:49:04,655 --> 01:49:07,225
No, not like that.

1094
01:49:07,275 --> 01:49:10,105
What do you mean Alcicek Hatun?

1095
01:49:12,995 --> 01:49:15,755
Okay, you don't love me.

1096
01:49:15,995 --> 01:49:18,525
Okay, you won't see me again.

1097
01:49:23,415 --> 01:49:25,195
But don't do this.

1098
01:49:27,655 --> 01:49:29,505
My wound is recent.

1099
01:49:29,735 --> 01:49:32,565
Can't you see that it's bleeding
with every look of yours?

1100
01:49:35,105 --> 01:49:37,285
Come on don't give me that look!

1101
01:49:38,655 --> 01:49:40,935
I don't understand what you want me to do.

1102
01:49:41,275 --> 01:49:42,625
What do I do?

1103
01:49:42,695 --> 01:49:44,545
Shall I leave Yenisehir?

1104
01:49:45,195 --> 01:49:48,045
I can't leave, I have a job.

1105
01:49:49,815 --> 01:49:51,585
That's what I am talking about.

1106
01:49:52,375 --> 01:49:55,635
You have a job, you have a job...

1107
01:49:55,815 --> 01:49:57,195
You have your mother.

1108
01:49:57,205 --> 01:49:58,775
And I have my mother.

1109
01:50:00,575 --> 01:50:02,395
It's just impossible.

1110
01:50:04,475 --> 01:50:07,025
You're playing with me, Alcicek.

1111
01:50:09,965 --> 01:50:11,795
And I will not allow this.

1112
01:50:23,795 --> 01:50:25,355
Aktemur!

1113
01:50:39,395 --> 01:50:40,955
Aktemur?

1114
01:50:57,045 --> 01:50:58,785
Did you say my name?

1115
01:51:00,285 --> 01:51:01,855
Is what I heard true?

1116
01:51:01,905 --> 01:51:03,745
I couldn't throw away the earrings.

1117
01:51:05,395 --> 01:51:07,445
But I couldn't wear them either.

1118
01:51:10,925 --> 01:51:13,425
I put them on my belt and walked around.

1119
01:51:15,925 --> 01:51:17,625
What is the meaning of this?

1120
01:51:20,595 --> 01:51:22,135
Don't take your looks away.

1121
01:51:26,665 --> 01:51:28,405
You hit me with them.

1122
01:51:29,985 --> 01:51:31,765
Don't run away now.

1123
01:51:34,095 --> 01:51:36,665
And you feel something for me, right?

1124
01:51:40,025 --> 01:51:41,815
Do you mean this?

1125
01:51:46,255 --> 01:51:47,565
You have a feeling.

1126
01:51:49,085 --> 01:51:50,805
Your eyes say so.

1127
01:51:52,985 --> 01:51:54,825
I want to hear it too.

1128
01:52:01,325 --> 01:52:03,825
What would change if I said
I have feelings for you?

1129
01:52:05,915 --> 01:52:08,775
The man who gave up on his love
when I rejected him for once!

1130
01:52:08,985 --> 01:52:11,445
How will he cope with the challanges
on our way?

1131
01:52:31,595 --> 01:52:33,465
Do you think I backed off?

1132
01:52:34,855 --> 01:52:37,935
Because I didn't see you
and your face?

1133
01:52:38,545 --> 01:52:40,135
I have the feeling.

1134
01:52:40,905 --> 01:52:44,215
Even if you weren't there and you
didn't feel anything for me...

1135
01:52:46,725 --> 01:52:48,075
My love is with me.

1136
01:52:49,325 --> 01:52:50,985
Even if my soul leaves my body...

1137
01:52:53,475 --> 01:52:55,575
Even if I die, my love is mine.

1138
01:52:59,425 --> 01:53:00,805
Also...

1139
01:53:02,715 --> 01:53:04,475
You love me too.

1140
01:53:05,245 --> 01:53:09,305
Love is heaven's bliss, Alcicek Hatun.

1141
01:53:11,455 --> 01:53:15,805
You love me, right?

1142
01:53:19,335 --> 01:53:20,485
I do.

1143
01:53:24,475 --> 01:53:26,265
I have feelings for you, Aktemur.

1144
01:53:28,505 --> 01:53:30,385
But this road is very bumpy.

1145
01:53:32,865 --> 01:53:34,725
You stopped with only a word of mine.

1146
01:53:34,895 --> 01:53:38,755
How will you face my mother
in this difficult path?

1147
01:53:39,265 --> 01:53:41,565
Nothing is more difficult
than your absence.

1148
01:53:41,565 --> 01:53:42,915
I will face them.

1149
01:53:43,565 --> 01:53:45,585
I think of my mom even now.

1150
01:53:45,785 --> 01:53:48,575
Do you know what would happen
if she saw us now together?

1151
01:53:49,475 --> 01:53:51,205
It would be bloody

1152
01:53:53,055 --> 01:53:55,085
Even if we get together...

1153
01:53:55,625 --> 01:53:57,395
She will not leave us alone.

1154
01:53:57,985 --> 01:53:59,665
We'd be miserable, Aktemur.

1155
01:54:01,445 --> 01:54:02,975
Just say it.

1156
01:54:05,005 --> 01:54:06,325
Say my name.

1157
01:54:08,355 --> 01:54:10,155
Say it again.

1158
01:54:13,755 --> 01:54:16,755
I'm telling you we'll be miserable,
what are you talking about?

1159
01:54:20,355 --> 01:54:22,565
We're already miserable, Alcicek Hatun!

1160
01:54:31,465 --> 01:54:33,965
If we are going to be miserable
either way...

1161
01:54:34,325 --> 01:54:39,405
Though, I think we will not be
if we get together.

1162
01:54:40,025 --> 01:54:42,885
But in your persepective...

1163
01:54:43,335 --> 01:54:45,765
Why are we being miserable
while we are seperated?

1164
01:54:46,235 --> 01:54:49,075
Let's be miserable together.

1165
01:54:51,965 --> 01:54:53,785
How will this happen?

1166
01:55:01,935 --> 01:55:05,645
Near Kopruhisar

1167
01:55:11,185 --> 01:55:13,705
Open the map, Gurbuz.

1168
01:55:18,595 --> 01:55:25,475
My Bey, this is the most secret way
to Kupruhisar through the Eagle's Nest

1169
01:55:27,375 --> 01:55:28,695
Is Cerkutay there?

1170
01:55:28,945 --> 01:55:31,235
He's there as you commanded, my Bey.

1171
01:55:32,315 --> 01:55:34,085
Not ony headquarters...

1172
01:55:34,815 --> 01:55:37,935
Rather, secret paths must be found to
Bilecik and Karacahisar.

1173
01:55:39,495 --> 01:55:43,175
But the most important place is Inegol.
We have to come from Inegol without being seen.

1174
01:55:44,555 --> 01:55:47,755
Turgut Bey was training
his alps for the war.

1175
01:55:47,945 --> 01:55:50,235
He has our catapults.

1176
01:55:51,255 --> 01:55:52,965
Where is Turgut Bey?

1177
01:55:53,035 --> 01:55:54,825
Hasn't he come yet?

1178
01:55:57,045 --> 01:55:59,135
We haven't heard from him, my Bey.

1179
01:56:01,985 --> 01:56:04,495
Although he knew we'd be exploring!

1180
01:56:10,815 --> 01:56:12,385
He's either late...

1181
01:56:13,625 --> 01:56:15,675
...or hasn't even set off.

1182
01:56:20,345 --> 01:56:21,915
We set off already.

1183
01:56:22,315 --> 01:56:25,015
The ones who look behind
cannot see their future.

1184
01:56:25,325 --> 01:56:26,645
Let's go.

1185
01:56:27,285 --> 01:56:29,145
Now let's keep exploring.

1186
01:56:52,545 --> 01:56:54,595
May I come in, my bey?

1187
01:56:56,985 --> 01:56:58,495
Come in, Kutan.

1188
01:57:07,505 --> 01:57:11,915
Osman Bey went out with his alps to explore
before the conquest of Kopruhisar.

1189
01:57:13,045 --> 01:57:15,155
Alps are waiting for the command.

1190
01:57:15,685 --> 01:57:17,455
Won't we go, my Bey?

1191
01:57:21,605 --> 01:57:24,465
Osman Bey doesn't need us, Kotan.

1192
01:57:29,565 --> 01:57:32,625
We are the men of war.

1193
01:57:33,565 --> 01:57:35,765
However, we always stand with the right.

1194
01:57:38,235 --> 01:57:39,775
I see now...

1195
01:57:41,005 --> 01:57:44,425
...that Osman Bey doesn't give the pie
to the deserver.

1196
01:57:45,425 --> 01:57:50,155
He does not see his brothers,
who fought with him for years.

1197
01:57:52,445 --> 01:57:55,145
As a result, he doesn't know
our value, Kutan.

1198
01:57:58,495 --> 01:58:04,465
We punish those who do not know
our value by our absence

1199
01:58:06,485 --> 01:58:08,125
What are we going to do, my Bey?

1200
01:58:08,385 --> 01:58:10,355
Will we abandon the war?

1201
01:58:13,125 --> 01:58:15,255
Don't you know your Turgut Bey?

1202
01:58:17,015 --> 01:58:21,525
Will we step back from the war just
because we don't agree with Osman Bey?

1203
01:58:21,745 --> 01:58:25,935
This world is full of infidels
whose throats must be cut off.

1204
01:58:26,535 --> 01:58:28,865
Let the soldiers be ready, Kutan.

1205
01:58:28,935 --> 01:58:31,225
We must continue on the road.

1206
01:58:32,865 --> 01:58:34,065
Your command, my Bey.

1207
01:58:39,635 --> 01:58:41,765
Whether with Osman Bey...

1208
01:58:43,615 --> 01:58:45,185
...or without him.

1209
01:59:31,925 --> 01:59:33,475
Olof.

1210
01:59:37,345 --> 01:59:38,855
Remus.

1211
01:59:39,215 --> 01:59:41,735
The Emperor's loyal commander.

1212
01:59:53,475 --> 01:59:55,215
Olof.

1213
01:59:59,515 --> 02:00:01,675
Your end is near, Olof.

1214
02:00:03,495 --> 02:00:05,875
The tricks you've made
against Kantakuzenos...

1215
02:00:06,455 --> 02:00:07,985
They're all revealed!

1216
02:00:08,795 --> 02:00:10,665
Nothing is over yet.

1217
02:00:18,755 --> 02:00:23,345
Osman Bey will make Kantakuzenos
talk by force.

1218
02:00:24,795 --> 02:00:27,385
The Emperor will know everything.

1219
02:00:28,485 --> 02:00:29,805
And you...

1220
02:00:35,355 --> 02:00:36,865
Kantakuzenos.

1221
02:00:37,395 --> 02:00:38,935
We must save him.

1222
02:00:39,425 --> 02:00:41,795
Otherwise, Osman will finish him.

1223
02:00:59,185 --> 02:01:00,505
Mother.

1224
02:01:01,815 --> 02:01:03,605
Where have you been, daughter?

1225
02:01:03,685 --> 02:01:05,205
Why did you even come?

1226
02:01:05,275 --> 02:01:07,865
Mother, the tent work took me forever,
so I got late.

1227
02:01:08,065 --> 02:01:10,575
Come on, you relax,
and I'll take care of the stall.

1228
02:01:13,015 --> 02:01:16,045
What is with you?
Why are you so happy?

1229
02:01:18,385 --> 02:01:21,465
Nothing.
What can it be, mother?

1230
02:01:22,035 --> 02:01:24,075
I heard about the throne for my father.

1231
02:01:24,905 --> 02:01:26,605
Why are you surprised?

1232
02:01:27,265 --> 02:01:30,835
Can they find someone better
than your father for the throne?

1233
02:01:41,745 --> 02:01:44,135
Don't keep me busy, I have a job.

1234
02:02:18,205 --> 02:02:19,735
Ulgen Hatun.

1235
02:02:19,755 --> 02:02:21,345
Aktemur Bey!

1236
02:02:23,295 --> 02:02:24,845
What's going on?

1237
02:02:27,705 --> 02:02:30,475
Tell me what's happening!
I saw you!

1238
02:02:30,475 --> 02:02:32,475
I saw how you looked at each other!

1239
02:02:36,625 --> 02:02:38,315
Alcicek loves me.

1240
02:02:38,805 --> 02:02:40,855
What did you say, my Bey?
What?

1241
02:03:07,885 --> 02:03:09,425
Attention!

1242
02:03:09,475 --> 02:03:11,575
Valide Ismahan Sultan!

1243
02:04:20,295 --> 02:04:22,155
They didn't inform us beforehand.

1244
02:04:22,595 --> 02:04:24,625
Do you think she came with good news?

1245
02:04:24,885 --> 02:04:26,975
I don't know, Bala.

1246
02:04:27,435 --> 02:04:29,465
After the conquest...

1247
02:04:30,465 --> 02:04:32,165
Whatever...

1248
02:04:32,315 --> 02:04:34,505
Let's call the good.

1249
02:05:04,215 --> 02:05:05,935
Come on, come on quickly!

1250
02:05:40,250 --> 02:05:42,820
Welcome Ismahan Hatun.

1251
02:05:43,340 --> 02:05:45,090
Welcome.

1252
02:05:45,090 --> 02:05:50,770
Osman Bey's Hatuns
Malhun Hatun and Bala Hatun.

1253
02:07:24,610 --> 02:07:26,870
Where is Osman Bey?

1254
02:07:27,760 --> 02:07:30,590
He didn't bother himself to welcome us.

1255
02:07:30,720 --> 02:07:32,250
Not at all.

1256
02:07:32,550 --> 02:07:34,310
Osman Bey is not here.

1257
02:07:34,490 --> 02:07:40,120
If he had been informed about your arrival,
he'd have arranged a ceremony for you.

1258
02:07:46,580 --> 02:07:50,400
You've come a long way,
you must be tired. Let me show your room.

1259
02:07:50,580 --> 02:07:52,970
We didn't come here to rest, Malhun Hatun.

1260
02:07:53,280 --> 02:07:55,570
State business cannot be postponed.

1261
02:07:59,980 --> 02:08:02,500
Of course, Ismahan Hatun.

1262
02:08:02,750 --> 02:08:07,360
State business cannot be postponed,
thus Osman Bey doesn't stay in the mansion.

1263
02:08:07,720 --> 02:08:10,670
He keeps conquering new lands.

1264
02:08:11,310 --> 02:08:13,780
This is why I am here.

1265
02:08:17,340 --> 02:08:20,400
While Osman Bey fights
one war after another...

1266
02:08:21,010 --> 02:08:24,270
...he must have gone blind.

1267
02:08:26,770 --> 02:08:33,770
He became unable to see in which direction
he runs and what he destroys.

1268
02:08:35,380 --> 02:08:37,400
Someone has to stop him.

1269
02:08:42,000 --> 02:08:44,010
Now let's get to the main topic.

1270
02:08:46,630 --> 02:08:48,770
Where's Kantakouzanos?

1271
02:09:02,130 --> 02:09:06,260
Gurbuz, we saw what you said
with our own eyes.

1272
02:09:06,870 --> 02:09:08,940
Kopruhisar is protected very well.

1273
02:09:09,250 --> 02:09:13,520
However, there has never been an obstacle
to stop Turks.

1274
02:09:13,730 --> 02:09:15,320
For sure, my Bey!

1275
02:09:15,860 --> 02:09:20,960
We will take down all and each of them.
We'll fly our flag on these lands!

1276
02:09:24,020 --> 02:09:25,800
Our work here is done.

1277
02:09:26,110 --> 02:09:29,250
Come on alps, we will go to Yenişehir.

1278
02:09:30,340 --> 02:09:31,670
Go!

1279
02:09:54,800 --> 02:09:56,150
Get out.

1280
02:10:11,090 --> 02:10:16,450
The one who doesn't know what being a leader
means doesn't know his limits either.

1281
02:10:17,950 --> 02:10:22,360
Has any of you ever heard or seen a prince is
being kept as a prisoner for such a long time?

1282
02:10:24,500 --> 02:10:25,950
You are right.

1283
02:10:27,200 --> 02:10:31,110
It amazes me to talk to someone
in this land who thinks like that.

1284
02:10:32,350 --> 02:10:36,270
I have always faced enmity while I just
wanted the alliance since I came.

1285
02:10:36,930 --> 02:10:39,780
Those times are over, Kantakouzanos.

1286
02:10:41,170 --> 02:10:43,700
Who are you and what do you want from me?

1287
02:10:45,410 --> 02:10:49,570
I am the mother of Aladdin,
the Sultan of Seljuq state.

1288
02:10:50,670 --> 02:10:52,210
I am Ismihan Sultan.

1289
02:10:54,900 --> 02:10:57,950
And you are the heir of the
Byzantine throne, Kantakouzanos.

1290
02:10:59,750 --> 02:11:04,130
The name of the Seljuk
state reaches beyond borders.

1291
02:11:05,650 --> 02:11:08,690
Our relationship with
Byzantium has been around for a long time

1292
02:11:09,810 --> 02:11:11,830
And we know each other very well.

1293
02:11:14,050 --> 02:11:16,090
We made peace at times.

1294
02:11:16,660 --> 02:11:18,950
We fought at times.

1295
02:11:20,560 --> 02:11:24,150
Now is the time to agree.

1296
02:11:27,570 --> 02:11:29,340
The two states shouldn't...

1297
02:11:29,410 --> 02:11:35,230
...allow men like Osman rise.

1298
02:11:36,290 --> 02:11:41,280
Beys like Osman benefitted from wars
between Byzantine and Seljuqs the most.

1299
02:11:42,370 --> 02:11:44,910
The more we weaken,
the more they strengthten.

1300
02:11:45,550 --> 02:11:50,710
He dared to arrest a Byzantine
prince like me.

1301
02:11:52,710 --> 02:11:56,230
Let's teach them their limit
so that we can be stronger

1302
02:11:57,780 --> 02:12:01,910
We'll agree, Kantakouzanos, we'll agree.

1303
02:12:03,830 --> 02:12:06,130
Now I have to get you out of here.

1304
02:12:07,350 --> 02:12:09,310
You are no use when you are a captive.

1305
02:12:14,710 --> 02:12:16,350
This is not good.

1306
02:12:16,870 --> 02:12:18,350
What do we do now?

1307
02:12:18,580 --> 02:12:19,860
I don't know Bala.

1308
02:12:20,450 --> 02:12:23,860
But we can't quarrel with Sultan
Ismihan at a time like this.

1309
02:12:46,100 --> 02:12:48,610
Stop, where are you taking him?

1310
02:13:07,790 --> 02:13:10,020
Your time has come too.

1311
02:13:14,190 --> 02:13:15,710
Attack!

1312
02:14:20,400 --> 02:14:23,470
First you, then your owner.

1313
02:14:23,810 --> 02:14:28,310
This will be the end of you
if you come to my land.

1314
02:14:40,820 --> 02:14:44,690
Kantakouzanos is free.

1315
02:14:47,170 --> 02:14:49,890
We can't allow this when
Osman Bey is not here.

1316
02:14:49,890 --> 02:14:51,630
This is not right.

1317
02:14:51,630 --> 02:14:53,760
You can't teach me what is right, Hatun.

1318
02:14:57,200 --> 02:14:57,910
Take him.

1319
02:14:58,160 --> 02:15:03,570
I will never forget what you made me
go through and how you hosted me

1320
02:15:04,510 --> 02:15:08,240
Enjoy your life until we meet again.

1321
02:15:40,080 --> 02:15:41,910
Go to Olof quickly.

1322
02:15:42,640 --> 02:15:46,100
Tell him Kantakouzanos has been released.

1323
02:16:10,870 --> 02:16:12,820
Bring Kantakouzanos
to the meeting, Boran.

1324
02:16:13,510 --> 02:16:14,870
Boran.

1325
02:16:15,570 --> 02:16:16,870
My Bey.

1326
02:16:16,920 --> 02:16:18,790
Kantakouzanos is not in jail.

1327
02:16:20,390 --> 02:16:22,100
They set him free.

1328
02:16:22,800 --> 02:16:24,600
What do you say, Bala?

1329
02:16:30,560 --> 02:16:32,270
Who did this?

1330
02:16:37,549 --> 02:16:39,129
Who did it?

1331
02:17:06,610 --> 02:17:08,930
Who released my captive?

1332
02:17:25,120 --> 02:17:30,450
Konya's Sultan Aladdin's mother
Ismihan Sultan!

1333
02:17:32,989 --> 02:17:34,568
Whoever you are!

1334
02:17:37,830 --> 02:17:41,409
The prisoner is my prisoner
and the city is my city.

1335
02:17:48,260 --> 02:17:50,290
Only my judgment runs here.

1336
02:18:07,520 --> 02:18:12,318
And I will rip out the heart of anyone
who draws his sword on my property.

1337
02:18:14,030 --> 02:18:15,568
Osman Bey.

1338
02:18:17,058 --> 02:18:18,409
Don't cross your limits!

1339
02:18:30,228 --> 02:18:33,440
As long as Konya has a Sultan...

1340
02:18:33,489 --> 02:18:36,580
Everything you have is ours!

1341
02:18:42,260 --> 02:18:46,350
And if we draw the sword, then this
means that we are on our land!

1342
02:18:47,440 --> 02:18:51,030
Don't you dare!

1343
02:18:54,549 --> 02:18:57,620
Don't try to take what's
mine, Ismahan Hatun.

1344
02:18:59,170 --> 02:19:04,080
Osman Bey, if you are a Bey under me,
you'll obey me!

1345
02:19:07,139 --> 02:19:10,318
If you say that you are the state...

1346
02:19:11,549 --> 02:19:16,549
Then you'll lose all the tribes you rule!

1347
02:19:18,870 --> 02:19:21,299
I warned you not to
try taking what is mine.

1348
02:19:22,469 --> 02:19:24,478
And now you set your eyes
on my tribe

1349
02:19:25,299 --> 02:19:26,850
Hatun!

1350
02:19:27,909 --> 02:19:32,030
I break the hand that reaches to my land,
and pluck out the eye that rests on it!

1351
02:19:38,159 --> 02:19:39,989
Everyone shall know their limit.

1352
02:19:40,430 --> 02:19:42,419
And I will teach you if you don't know!

1353
02:19:53,910 --> 02:19:55,210
By the way...

1354
02:19:56,350 --> 02:19:57,850
I am the Bey.

1355
02:19:58,860 --> 02:20:00,450
And I am the state!

1356
02:20:00,450 --> 02:20:02,230
I am the state!

1357
02:20:06,840 --> 02:20:23,960
